rectories","type":"command_run"},"type":"compressed"},"obs_mqv7fgx0_ca9b7b2b7370":{"observation":{"concepts":["project structure","python codebase discovery","modular architecture"],"confidence":0.65,"facts":[],"files":["/Users/xnch/xnchSystems/nexi/nexi/main.py","/Users/xnch/xnchSystems/nexi/nexi/pipeline/pipeline.py","/Users/xnch/xnchSystems/xnch/xnch/agents/codegen_loop.py"],"id":"obs_mqv7fgx0_ca9b7b2b7370","importance":3,"narrative":"Executed a find command to map the codebase. This establishes the project structure for both the nexi and xnch systems, revealing the modular architecture of the pipeline and agent components.","sessionId":"283b9ba1-0eba-4a0c-ba9d-0cf00eb4bc4b","subtitle":"Scanned xnch and nexi directories for Python source files","timestamp":"2026-06-26T17:28:01.338Z","title":"Project file structure discovery","type":"discovery"},"type":"compressed"},"obs_mqv7fpxz_57cd74ad1bc0":{"observation":{"concepts":["Redis-based stream processing","TTL-based caching","Memory hierarchy (Layer 0)","Asynchronous Redis patterns"],"confidence":1,"facts":["Uses Redis for short-lived (TTL) storage of raw perception signals.","Implements `write_perception` with auto-expiry (default 60s).","Implements `read_recent` using Redis SCAN and pipelining for efficient retrieval.","Implements `flush_to_working_memory` to promote processed data from Redis to working memory."],"files":["/Users/xnch/xnchSystems/xnch/xnch/memory/sensory_buffer.py"],"id":"obs_mqv7fpxz_57cd74ad1bc0","importance":4,"narrative":"The file defines the `SensoryBuffer` class, which acts as Layer 0 of the memory hierarchy. It provides a way to ingest and expire raw signals before they are summarized and moved to higher-level memory.","sessionId":"283b9ba1-0eba-4a0c-ba9d-0cf00eb4bc4b","subtitle":"Implementation of Redis-based sensory buffer for raw perception signals","timestamp":"2026-06-26T17:28:13.032Z","title":"Read sensory_buffer.py","type":"file_read"},"type":"compressed"},"obs_mqv7fq79_c14d686c3724":{"observation":{"concepts":["Redis session management","Distributed cache pattern","TTL-based context expiration","Async Redis operations"],"confidence":1,"facts":["Implementation of `WorkingMemory` class using Redis (aioredis).","Uses Redis hashes for session-specific key-value pairs.","Uses Redis lists (`rpush`/`lrange`) to store conversation turns.","Supports session-based TTL (default 3600s).","Key structure: `session:{session_id}:{key}</key>`."],"files":["/Users/xnch/xnchSystems/xnch/xnch/memory/working_memory.py"],"id":"obs_mqv7fq79_c14d686c3724","importance":4,"narrative":"The file defines the primary mechanism for managing active session context. It handles both structured metadata (via hashes) and chronological chat history (via lists) within Redis.","sessionId":"283b9ba1-0eba-4a0c-ba9d-0cf00eb4bc4b","subtitle":"Examining Redis-based session context management","timestamp":"2026-06-26T17:28:13.372Z","title":"Read working_memory.py","type":"file_read"},"type":"compressed"},"obs_mqv7fqum_dfdef85e0a3e":{"observation":{"concepts":["episodic memory","pgvector","vector embeddings","semantic search","metadata management"],"confidence":1,"facts":["Implements PgEpisodicStore using PostgreSQL + pgvector semantics.","Uses agentmemory (ChromaDB-based) for underlying storage in the 'episodes' category.","Supports storing episodes with metadata: type, raw_text, summary, importance, and timestamps.","Retrieval logic handles both embedding-based search and text-based search with similarity thresholds."],"files":["/Users/xnch/xnchSystems/xnch/xnch/memory/pg_episodic_store.py"],"id":"obs_mqv7fqum_dfdef85e0a3e","importance":4,"narrative":"Read the implementation of the episodic memory store to understand how long-term 'episodes' are structured and retrieved. This file defines the schema and interaction patterns for the second layer of memory.","sessionId":"283b9ba1-0eba-4a0c-ba9d-0cf00eb4bc4b","subtitle":"Inspecting Layer 2 episodic memory implementation","timestamp":"2026-06-26T17:28:14.211Z","title":"Read pg_episodic_store.py","type":"file_read"},"type":"compressed"},"obs_mqv7fr3t_b0464ddab37f":{"observation":{"concepts":["Semantic Graph Store","Entity-Relationship modeling","Layer 3 memory","Graph-based retrieval"],"confidence":1,"facts":["GraphStore implements Layer 3 memory using agentmemory categories.","Uses ENTITIES_CATEGORY (\"entities\") and RELATIONS_CATEGORY (\"relations\") for storage.","Supports upserting entities and relations with metadata.","Supports querying entity connections via relationship lookups.","Integrates with an optional relationship_store for asynchronous updates."],"files":["/Users/xnch/xnchSystems/xnch/xnch/memory/graph_store.py"],"id":"obs_mqv7fr3t_b0464ddab37f","importance":6,"narrative":"The file defines the GraphStore class, which manages a semantic graph of entities and relationships. This provides the structure for interconnected memory within the agent system.","sessionId":"283b9ba1-0eba-4a0c-ba9d-0cf00eb4bc4b","subtitle":"Inspecting implementation of Semantic Graph Store","timestamp":"2026-06-26T17:28:14.541Z","title":"Read graph_store.py","type":"file_read"},"type":"compressed"},"obs_mqv7fr3t_9059569f8332":{"observation":{"concepts":["PostgreSQL asyncpg","Entity relationship tracking","Connection pooling","Upsert pattern"],"confidence":1,"facts":["Uses asyncpg for PostgreSQL connectivity","Implements RelationshipRecord dataclass for entity relationships","Upsert logic uses ON CONFLICT for strength and evidence array appending","RelationshipStore manages a connection pool with min_size=1, max_size=5"],"files":["/Users/xnch/xnchSystems/xnch/xnch/memory/relationship_store.py"],"id":"obs_mqv7fr3t_9059569f8332","importance":3,"narrative":"The file contains the implementation of the relationship memory store, which tracks connections between entities in a PostgreSQL database. It allows for updating relationship strength and accumulating evidence via upsert operations.","sessionId":"283b9ba1-0eba-4a0c-ba9d-0cf00eb4bc4b","subtitle":"Inspecting PostgreSQL-backed relationship memory implementation","timestamp":"2026-06-26T17:28:14.541Z","title":"Read relationship_store.py","type":"file_read"},"type":"compressed"},"obs_mqv7fre3_873e2de54b8e":{"observation":{"concepts":["PostgreSQL connection pooling","Data quarantine pattern","Async database transactions"],"confidence":1,"facts":["Uses asyncpg for PostgreSQL connection pooling","Implements quarantine() to insert memories into 'quarantine_memories' table","Implements release_to_memory() to move items from quarantine to active memory","Tracks metadata: reason, actor role, trust level, and importance"],"files":["/Users/xnch/xnchSystems/xnch/xnch/memory/quarantine_store.py"],"id":"obs_mqv7fre3_873e2de54b8e","importance":3,"narrative":"The agent inspected the QuarantineStore class to understand how unverified or suspicious memories are isolated and managed in the PostgreSQL database.","sessionId":"283b9ba1-0eba-4a0c-ba9d-0cf00eb4bc4b","subtitle":"Inspecting the database-backed quarantine storage logic","timestamp":"2026-06-26T17:28:14.914Z","title":"Read QuarantineStore implementation","type":"file_read"},"type":"compressed"},"obs_mqv7fuij_fe9acf94a943":{"observation":{"concepts":["LLM routing","request classification","heuristics-based routing","caching/memory-based retrieval"],"confidence":1,"facts":["Implements a request routing mechanism between 'gemma4-local' and 'claude-judgment'.","Routing decisions are based on complexity scores, privacy sensitivity, and intent class (EXECUTION vs DECISION).","Uses a memory-based lookup (search_memory) to recall previous routing decisions for identical inputs.","Complexity is computed based on input length, presence of multi-step keywords, and presence of code snippets.","Decisions are persisted to 'routing-decisions' memory for future retrieval."],"files":["/Users/xnch/xnch/routing/classifier.py"],"id":"obs_mqv7fuij_fe9acf94a943","importance":5,"narrative":"The file contains the core logic for a request classifier that routes LLM tasks to either a local model or a cloud model. It uses metadata-driven heuristics and historical memory to optimize for latency, cost, and privacy.","sessionId":"283b9ba1-0eba-4a0c-ba9d-0cf00eb4bc4b","subtitle":"/Users/xnch/xnch/routing/classifier.py","timestamp":"2026-06-26T17:28:18.957Z","title":"Read routing classifier logic","type":"file_read"},"type":"compressed"},"obs_mqv7fv3z_304b47e3368d":{"observation":{"concepts":["Role-based access control (RBAC)","Trust-based authorization","FastAPI middleware/decorators","Security trust model"],"confidence":1,"facts":["Defines TrustLevel enum ranging from UNTRUSTED (1) to SYSTEM (5).","ACTOR_TRUST_MAP assigns specific roles (nexi, openclaw, etc.) to trust levels.","Implements a @requires_trust decorator that validates the 'X-Actor-Role' header in the FastAPI Request object.","Throws 403 Forbidden if the actor's trust level is below the required minimum."],"files":["/Users/xnch/xnchSystems/xnch/xnch/security/trust_model.py"],"id":"obs_mqv7fv3z_304b47e3368d","importance":6,"narrative":"The file defines the core security architecture for actor-based authorization within the system. It uses a decorator pattern to enforce minimum trust levels based on request headers.","sessionId":"283b9ba1-0eba-4a0c-ba9d-0cf00eb4bc4b","subtitle":"Inspecting the TrustLevel enum and access control decorators","timestamp":"2026-06-26T17:28:19.732Z","title":"Read security trust model implementation","type":"file_read"},"type":"compressed"},"obs_mqv7fvea_1850c22c9afd":{"observation":{"concepts":["prompt injection prevention","regex-based security scanning","security auditing"],"confidence":1,"facts":["/Users/xnch/xnch/security/injection_guard.py implements regex-based detection of prompt injection attacks.","Uses predefined INJECTION_PATTERNS to scan text for common jailbreak phrases like \"ignore previous instructions\" or \"DAN mode\".","Integrates with EventLog to emit warnings when risk score exceeds 0.1.","Calculates risk_score based on the ratio of matched patterns to total patterns."],"files":["/Users/xnch/xnch/security/injection_guard.py"],"id":"obs_mqv7fvea_1850c22c9afd","importance":5,"narrative":"The file was read to understand the implementation of the security guard module. This module is responsible for detecting and logging potential prompt injection attempts within the system.","sessionId":"283b9ba1-0eba-4a0c-ba9d-0cf00eb4bc4b","subtitle":"Inspecting security pattern matching for prompt injection prevention","timestamp":"2026-06-26T17:28:20.104Z","title":"Read injection_guard.py","type":"file_read"},"type":"compressed"},"obs_mqv7fvp4_5c6b1379738c":{"observation":{"concepts":["input injection scanning","trust-based access control","episodic memory security","trust model"],"confidence":1,"facts":["File: /Users/xnch/xnchSystems/xnch/xnch/security/memory_guard.py","Uses scan_input from injection_guard to check for injection patterns","Enforces trust level requirements for writing to episodic store","TrustLevel.TRUSTED_AGENT is the minimum required level for direct writes","Defines QUARANTINE_TABLE as \"quarantine_memories\""],"files":["/Users/xnch/xnchSystems/xnch/xnch/security/memory_guard.py"],"id":"obs_mqv7fvp4_5c6b1379738c","importance":5,"narrative":"Read the implementation of the memory guard module which handles security validation for memory writes. The module performs injection scanning and verifies the trust level of the actor before allowing writes to the episodic store.","sessionId":"283b9ba1-0eba-4a0c-ba9d-0cf00eb4bc4b","subtitle":"Inspecting memory write validation logic","timestamp":"2026-06-26T17:28:20.495Z","title":"Read security memory guard implementation","type":"file_read"},"type":"compressed"},"obs_mqv7fvzn_0d7846bdd4ee":{"observation":{"concepts":["role-based access control","security sandboxing","trust model","actor capabilities"],"confidence":1,"facts":["Defines ActorCapabilities dataclass with specific permission flags (write_memory, read_all_memory, etc.)","CAPABILITY_MAP maps TrustLevel to specific permission sets","Trust levels range from SYSTEM and OWNER to TRUSTED_AGENT, EXTERNAL_AGENT, and UNTRUSTED","get_capabilities() function resolves actor_role to capabilities via TrustLevel"],"files":["/Users/xnch/xnchSystems/xnch/xnch/security/actor_sandbox.py"],"id":"obs_mqv7fvzn_0d7846bdd4ee","importance":5,"narrative":"The file defines the security sandbox configuration, mapping various trust levels to specific system capabilities. This establishes the permission boundaries for different types of actors within the system.","sessionId":"283b9ba1-0eba-4a0c-ba9d-0cf00eb4bc4b","subtitle":"Examine security capabilities mapping for different trust levels","timestamp":"2026-06-26T17:28:20.873Z","title":"Read actor_sandbox.py","type":"file_read"},"type":"compressed"},"obs_mqv7fw8i_a39b443e593b":{"observation":{"concepts":["SQLite WAL mode","Schema migrations","aiosqlite","Relational schema design"],"confidence":1,"facts":["Uses SQLite with WAL mode and foreign key enforcement enabled.","Tables: actors (identity/capabilities), episodes (decision logs), patterns (learned behaviors), weight_configs (JSON weights), pending_weight_configs, policy_candidates, and system_state.","Primary keys and indices are defined for efficient querying of episodes and patterns.","Uses aiosqlite for asynchronous database operations."],"files":["/Users/xnch/xnchSystems/xnch/xnch/memory/db.py"],"id":"obs_mqv7fw8i_a39b443e593b","importance":4,"narrative":"The file defines the core database schema and initialization logic for the memory system. It includes tables for tracking actors, decision episodes, patterns, and configuration weights.","sessionId":"283b9ba1-0eba-4a0c-ba9d-0cf00eb4bc4b","subtitle":"Inspecting db.py for database structure and migrations","timestamp":"2026-06-26T17:28:21.192Z","title":"Read SQLite database schema definition","type":"file_read"},"type":"compressed"},"obs_mqv7fz4y_193606aa4e36":{"observation":{"concepts":["Voice Activity Detection (VAD)","Whisper Speech-to-Text","Asynchronous Redis integration","Audio buffer processing"],"confidence":1,"facts":["Uses Redis (aioredis) for storing perception payloads with a 60s TTL.","Implements speech-to-text using `faster_whisper` (WhisperModel).","Uses Silero VAD for voice activity detection.","Handles audio buffering and transcription in an asynchronous event loop using `run_in_executor`.","Uses Redis keys in the format `perception:voice:{perception_id}`."],"files":["/Users/xnch/xnchSystems/xnch/xnch/perception/voice_daemon.py"],"id":"obs_mqv7fz4y_193606aa4e36","importance":4,"narrative":"Read the source code for the voice daemon to understand how audio recording, transcription, and silence detection are managed. This file is a central component of the perception system.","sessionId":"283b9ba1-0eba-4a0c-ba9d-0cf00eb4bc4b","subtitle":"Examining the core implementation of the voice processing service","timestamp":"2026-06-26T17:28:24.951Z","title":"Read voice_daemon.py","type":"file_read"},"type":"compressed"},"obs_mqv7fzff_c8c47c998205":{"observation":{"concepts":["asynchronous model loading","vision-language models","Redis caching","moondream"],"confidence":1,"facts":["Uses moondream2 model for image captioning via run_in_executor.","Stores encoded vision descriptions in Redis with a 60-second TTL.","Implements an asynchronous lock to ensure single-instance model loading.","Payload includes perception_id, description, timestamp, and type."],"files":[],"id":"obs_mqv7fzff_c8c47c998205","importance":4,"narrative":"The file defines the VisionEncoder class, which processes screenshots using the moondream vision model. It uses Redis to cache the generated descriptions temporarily.","sessionId":"283b9ba1-0eba-4a0c-ba9d-0cf00eb4bc4b","subtitle":"Inspecting the VisionEncoder implementation","timestamp":"2026-06-26T17:28:25.330Z","title":"Read vision_encoder.py","type":"file_read"},"type":"compressed"},"obs_mqv7fzr5_484c063165db":{"observation":{"concepts":["file system watching","asyncio event loop","debouncing","watchdog library"],"confidence":1,"facts":["Uses watchdog.observers.Observer to monitor directory changes.","Implements a 5-second debounce mechanism to prevent rapid-fire events.","Dispatches file modification/creation events to a Kubernetes jobs URL via HTTP POST.","Uses asyncio.run_coroutine_threadsafe to bridge watchdog threads with the main asyncio loop."],"files":["/Users/xnch/xnch/xnch/perception/file_watcher.py"],"id":"obs_mqv7fzr5_484c063165db","importance":4,"narrative":"Read the implementation of FileWatcher to understand how file system changes are detected and propagated to the k8s jobs service. The class uses a debounce strategy and an HTTP client to notify a remote endpoint of modifications.","sessionId":"283b9ba1-0eba-4a0c-ba9d-0cf00eb4bc4b","subtitle":"Inspecting file watching and event dispatching logic","timestamp":"2026-06-26T17:28:25.752Z","title":"Read file_watcher.py","type":"file_read"},"type":"compressed"},"obs_mqv7g0be_6735cf60e150":{"observation":{"concepts":["attention filtering","activity monitoring","event-driven architecture","user idle detection"],"confidence":1,"facts":["Implements AttentionFilter class for monitoring user activity.","Tracks voice transcripts, screen pixel changes, and file saving events.","Triggers consolidation tasks when user idle timeout is exceeded.","Uses thresholds from settings for silence, screen diff, and idle duration."],"files":["/Users/xnch/xnch/xnch/perception/attention_filter.py"],"id":"obs_mqv7g0be_6735cf60e150","importance":5,"narrative":"The file defines the core logic for the perception layer's attention filtering. It evaluates environmental inputs (voice, screen, file system) to decide when to trigger system actions like gateway forwarding or data consolidation.","sessionId":"283b9ba1-0eba-4a0c-ba9d-0cf00eb4bc4b","subtitle":"Inspecting perception layer logic","timestamp":"2026-06-26T17:28:26.481Z","title":"Read attention_filter.py","type":"file_read"},"type":"compressed"},"obs_mqv7g0ma_7f848171071e":{"observation":{"concepts":["LLM observability","Langfuse integration","HTTP client instrumentation","Python singleton pattern"],"confidence":1,"facts":["Defines LangfuseClient for sending LLM traces to Langfuse ingestion API.","Uses httpx.Client for making asynchronous-ready HTTP requests.","Implements Basic Auth using public and secret keys from settings.","Calculates usage based on word counts (split) rather than actual tokenization.","Provides a singleton-style `get_client` and `trace_llm_call` utility functions."],"files":["/Users/xnch/xnchSystems/xnch/xnch/observability/langfuse_client.py"],"id":"obs_mqv7g0ma_7f848171071e","importance":3,"narrative":"Read the langfuse_client.py file to understand how LLM calls are being instrumented and sent to the observability backend. This is crucial for understanding the system's observability architecture.","sessionId":"283b9ba1-0eba-4a0c-ba9d-0cf00eb4bc4b","subtitle":"Inspecting observability client for LLM call tracing","timestamp":"2026-06-26T17:28:26.872Z","title":"Read Langfuse client implementation","type":"file_read"},"type":"compressed"},"obs_mqv7g0yx_d08f4a14219a":{"observation":{"concepts":["knowledge graph extraction","entity-relation triples","LLM-based information extraction","episodic memory"],"confidence":1,"facts":["Uses litellm/ollama/phi3:mini for triple extraction.","Extracts subject-relation-object triples from episodic memories.","Stores extracted triples into a GraphStore (GraphStore/PgEpisodicStore).","Identifies entities by id, name, and type."],"files":["/Users/xnch/xnchSystems/xnch/xnch/memory/graph_extractor.py"],"id":"obs_mqv7g0yx_d08f4a14219a","importance":5,"narrative":"The script parses recent episodes from episodic memory and uses an LLM to generate structured graph relations. These relations are then upserted into a persistent graph store.","sessionId":"283b9ba1-0eba-4a0c-ba9d-0cf00eb4bc4b","subtitle":"Inspecting LLM-based entity-relation extraction logic","timestamp":"2026-06-26T17:28:27.328Z","title":"Read graph_extractor.py","type":"file_read"},"type":"compressed"},"obs_mqv7g5ty_fd19f2422957":{"observation":{"concepts":["pattern extraction","Bayesian smoothing","episodic memory","APScheduler","data mining"],"confidence":1,"facts":["PatternExtractor runs as a 6h APScheduler job.","Queries PgEpisodicStore for decision episodes since last run.","Falls back to SQLite EpisodicStore if Postgres is unavailable.","Uses Bayesian-smoothed confidence for pattern upserts into PatternStore.","Groups episodes by (intent_class, action_type, entity_class, actor_role).","Uses SHA256 hashing for pattern signatures."],"files":["/Users/xnch/xnchSystems/xnch/xnch/learning/pattern_extractor.py"],"id":"obs_mqv7g5ty_fd19f2422957","importance":3,"narrative":"Read the implementation of PatternExtractor to understand how the system extracts and stores recurring interaction patterns. This is key to understanding the system's learning/memory loop.","sessionId":"283b9ba1-0eba-4a0c-ba9d-0cf00eb4bc4b","subtitle":"Inspecting periodic pattern extraction logic","timestamp":"2026-06-26T17:28:33.622Z","title":"Read pattern_extractor.py","type":"file_read"},"type":"compressed"},"obs_mqv7g69x_1e353f05c246":{"observation":{"concepts":["drift detection","weight adjustment","Pearson correlation","performance monitoring"],"confidence":1,"facts":["The ScoreAdapter class monitors accuracy drift in dimensions: policy_score, outcome_score, risk_score, and context_fit_score.","Drift is calculated by comparing 7-day rolling accuracy against a 30-day baseline.","If drift exceeds 0.05 and sample size is sufficient (>= 10), it proposes weight adjustments via POST /governance/weights/propose.","Accuracy is measured using Pearson correlation between predicted scores and actual outcomes (SUCCESS/FAILURE)."],"files":["/Users/xnch/xnchSystems/xnch/xnch/learning/score_adapter.py"],"id":"obs_mqv7g69x_1e353f05c246","importance":5,"narrative":"Read the score_adapter.py file to understand how the system detects model performance drift and automates weight re-tuning for different intent classes.","sessionId":"283b9ba1-0eba-4a0c-ba9d-0cf00eb4bc4b","subtitle":"Inspecting the weight adjustment logic for prediction accuracy","timestamp":"2026-06-26T17:28:34.202Z","title":"Read score_adapter.py","type":"file_read"},"type":"compressed"},"obs_mqv7g6my_41e07ff48d1e":{"observation":{"concepts":["LLM-driven policy generation","Policy DSL","Autonomous governance","Pattern-based rule generation"],"confidence":1,"facts":["The module generates policy DSL rules using an LLM based on low-success/high-confidence patterns from PatternStore.","Uses 'claude-judgment' model via a local LiteLLM proxy (localhost:4000).","Valid verdicts: ALLOW, ALLOW_WITH_WARNINGS, BLOCK, MODIFY, DEFER (DENY is forbidden).","Writes results to a SQLite table named 'policy_candidates' with status 'PENDING'.","Policy structure includes rule_id, priority, conditions (intent_class, action_type, entity_class, actor_role), and action (verdict, reason)."],"files":["/Users/xnch/xnchSystems/xnch/xnch/learning/policy_candidates.py"],"id":"obs_mqv7g6my_41e07ff48d1e","importance":5,"narrative":"Read the implementation of the PolicyCandidateGenerator. This class automates the proposal of new governance rules by analyzing existing failure patterns in the PatternStore and prompting an LLM to suggest YAML-based policy candidates.","sessionId":"283b9ba1-0eba-4a0c-ba9d-0cf00eb4bc4b","subtitle":"Inspecting the policy candidate generation logic","timestamp":"2026-06-26T17:28:34.671Z","title":"Read policy_candidates.py","type":"file_read"},"type":"compressed"},"obs_mqv7g6v5_0c4e05bb40c1":{"observation":{"concepts":["memory decay algorithm","episodic memory archiving","graph extraction","data consolidation"],"confidence":1,"facts":["The script performs summarization, graph extraction, decay calculation, and archiving.","Decay formula: importance * (e^(-0.1 * days)) * (1 + 0.1 * recall_count).","Memories with decay_score &lt; 0.1 are marked as archived.","Uses agentmemory for storage and retrieval of episodic data."],"files":["/Users/xnch/xnchSystems/xnch/xnch/jobs/consolidation.py"],"id":"obs_mqv7g6v5_0c4e05bb40c1","importance":5,"narrative":"The file defines a periodic consolidation job that manages memory lifecycle by calculating decay scores based on age and recall frequency, then archiving old, low-importance memories.","sessionId":"283b9ba1-0eba-4a0c-ba9d-0cf00eb4bc4b","subtitle":"Inspecting the background consolidation and decay logic","timestamp":"2026-06-26T17:28:34.967Z","title":"Read consolidation job script","type":"file_read"},"type":"compressed"},"obs_mqv7g761_d2e78039c109":{"observation":{"hookType":"post_tool_use","id":"obs_mqv7g761_d2e78039c109","raw":{"tool_input":{"file_path":"/Users/xnch/xnchSystems/xnch/xnch/memory/pattern_store.py"},"tool_name":"Read","tool_output":{"file":{"content":"\"\"\"Pattern Store — aggregated patterns derived from episodic history.\"\"\"\nimport json\nimport time\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom typing import Any\nfrom uuid import uuid4\n\nimport aiosqlite\n\n\nclass PatternStore:\n    def __init__(self, db_path: Path) -> None:\n        self._db = db_path\n\n    async def upsert_pattern(\n        self,\n        context_signature: str,\n        intent_class: str,\n        action_type: str,\n        entity_class: str,\n        actor_role: str,\n        success_rate: float,\n        confidence: float,\n        observation_count: int,\n        avg_prediction_delta: float | None,\n        extraction_run_id: str,\n    ) -> None:\n        now = time.time()\n        async with aiosqlite.connect(self._db) as db:\n            async with db.execute(\n                \"SELECT pattern_id FROM patterns WHERE context_signature = ?\",\n                (context_signature,),\n            ) as cursor:\n                row = await cursor.fetchone()\n\n            if row:\n                await db.execute(\n                    \"\"\"UPDATE patterns SET success_rate=?, confidence=?, observation_count=?,\n                       avg_prediction_delta=?, extraction_run_id=?, updated_at=?\n                       WHERE context_signature=?\"\"\",\n                    (success_rate, confidence, observation_count, avg_prediction_delta,\n                     extraction_run_id, now, context_signature),\n                )\n            else:\n                await db.execute(\n                    \"\"\"INSERT INTO patterns\n                       (pattern_id, context_signature, intent_class, action_type, entity_class,\n                        actor_role, success_rate, confidence, observation_count,\n                        avg_prediction_delta, extraction_run_id, created_at, updated_at)\n                       VALUES (?, ?, ?, ?, ?, ?, ?, ?, ?, ?, ?, ?, ?)\"\"\",\n                    (str(uuid4()), context_signature, intent_class, action_type, entity_class,\n                     actor_role, success_rate, confidence, observation_count,\n                     avg_prediction_delta, extraction_run_id, now, now),\n                )\n            await db.commit()\n\n    async def fetch_for_manifest(\n        self,\n        intent_class: str,\n        entity_class: str,\n        actor_role: str,\n        max_patterns: int = 10,\n    ) -> list[dict[str, Any]]:\n        async with aiosqlite.connect(self._db) as db:\n            db.row_factory = aiosqlite.Row\n            async with db.execute(\n                \"\"\"SELECT pattern_id, context_signature, success_rate, confidence, observation_count\n                   FROM patterns\n                   WHERE intent_class = ? AND entity_class = ? AND actor_role = ?\n                   ORDER BY confidence DESC LIMIT ?\"\"\",\n                (intent_class, entity_class, actor_role, max_patterns),\n            ) as cursor:\n                rows = await cursor.fetchall()\n        return [dict(r) for r in rows]\n\n    async def fetch_low_success(\n        self,\n        max_success_rate: float = 0.4,\n        min_confidence: float = 0.6,\n    ) -> list[dict[str, Any]]:\n        async with aiosqlite.connect(self._db) as db:\n            db.row_factory = aiosqlite.Row\n            async with db.execute(\n                \"\"\"SELECT * FROM patterns\n                   WHERE success_rate < ? AND confidence > ?\n                   ORDER BY confidence DESC\"\"\",\n                (max_success_rate, min_confidence),\n            ) as cursor:\n                rows = await cursor.fetchall()\n        return [dict(r) for r in rows]\n\n    async def fetch_all(self) -> list[dict[str, Any]]:\n        async with aiosqlite.connect(self._db) as db:\n            db.row_factory = aiosqlite.Row\n            async with db.execute(\"SELECT * FROM patterns\") as cursor:\n                rows = await cursor.fetchall()\n        return [dict(r) for r in rows]\n","filePath":"/Users/xnch/xnchSystems/xnch/xnch/memory/pattern_store.py","numLines":98,"startLine":1,"totalLines":98},"type":"text"}},"sessionId":"283b9ba1-0eba-4a0c-ba9d-0cf00eb4bc4b","timestamp":"2026-06-26T17:28:35.359Z","toolInput":{"file_path":"/Users/xnch/xnchSystems/xnch/xnch/memory/pattern_store.py"},"toolName":"Read","toolOutput":{"file":{"content":"\"\"\"Pattern Store — aggregated patterns derived from episodic history.\"\"\"\nimport json\nimport time\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom typing import Any\nfrom uuid import uuid4\n\nimport aiosqlite\n\n\nclass PatternStore:\n    def __init__(self, db_path: Path) -> None:\n        self._db = db_path\n\n    async def upsert_pattern(\n        self,\n        context_signature: str,\n        intent_class: str,\n        action_type: str,\n        entity_class: str,\n        actor_role: str,\n        success_rate: float,\n        confidence: float,\n        observation_count: int,\n        avg_prediction_delta: float | None,\n        extraction_run_id: str,\n    ) -> None:\n        now = time.time()\n        async with aiosqlite.connect(self._db) as db:\n            async with db.execute(\n                \"SELECT pattern_id FROM patterns WHERE context_signature = ?\",\n                (context_signature,),\n            ) as cursor:\n                row = await cursor.fetchone()\n\n            if row:\n                await db.execute(\n                    \"\"\"UPDATE patterns SET success_rate=?, confidence=?, observation_count=?,\n                       avg_prediction_delta=?, extraction_run_id=?, updated_at=?\n                       WHERE context_signature=?\"\"\",\n                    (success_rate, confidence, observation_count, avg_prediction_delta,\n                     extraction_run_id, now, context_signature),\n                )\n            else:\n                await db.execute(\n                    \"\"\"INSERT INTO patterns\n                       (pattern_id, context_signature, intent_class, action_type, entity_class,\n                        actor_role, success_rate, confidence, observation_count,\n                        avg_prediction_delta, extraction_run_id, created_at, updated_at)\n                       VALUES (?, ?, ?, ?, ?, ?, ?, ?, ?, ?, ?, ?, ?)\"\"\",\n                    (str(uuid4()), context_signature, intent_class, action_type, entity_class,\n                     actor_role, success_rate, confidence, observation_count,\n                     avg_prediction_delta, extraction_run_id, now, now),\n                )\n            await db.commit()\n\n    async def fetch_for_manifest(\n        self,\n        intent_class: str,\n        entity_class: str,\n        actor_role: str,\n        max_patterns: int = 10,\n    ) -> list[dict[str, Any]]:\n        async with aiosqlite.connect(self._db) as db:\n            db.row_factory = aiosqlite.Row\n            async with db.execute(\n                \"\"\"SELECT pattern_id, context_signature, success_rate, confidence, observation_count\n                   FROM patterns\n                   WHERE intent_class = ? AND entity_class = ? AND actor_role = ?\n                   ORDER BY confidence DESC LIMIT ?\"\"\",\n                (intent_class, entity_class, actor_role, max_patterns),\n            ) as cursor:\n                rows = await cursor.fetchall()\n        return [dict(r) for r in rows]\n\n    async def fetch_low_success(\n        self,\n        max_success_rate: float = 0.4,\n        min_confidence: float = 0.6,\n    ) -> list[dict[str, Any]]:\n        async with aiosqlite.connect(self._db) as db:\n            db.row_factory = aiosqlite.Row\n            async with db.execute(\n                \"\"\"SELECT * FROM patterns\n                   WHERE success_rate < ? AND confidence > ?\n                   ORDER BY confidence DESC\"\"\",\n                (max_success_rate, min_confidence),\n            ) as cursor:\n                rows = await cursor.fetchall()\n        return [dict(r) for r in rows]\n\n    async def fetch_all(self) -> list[dict[str, Any]]:\n        async with aiosqlite.connect(self._db) as db:\n            db.row_factory = aiosqlite.Row\n            async with db.execute(\"SELECT * FROM patterns\") as cursor:\n                rows = await cursor.fetchall()\n        return [dict(r) for r in rows]\n","filePath":"/Users/xnch/xnchSystems/xnch/xnch/memory/pattern_store.py","numLines":98,"startLine":1,"totalLines":98},"type":"text"}},"type":"raw"},"obs_mqv7g7fk_5e182faeb045":{"observation":{"hookType":"post_tool_use","id":"obs_mqv7g7fk_5e182faeb045","raw":{"tool_input":{"file_path":"/Users/xnch/xnchSystems/xnch/xnch/memory/episodic_store.py"},"tool_name":"Read","tool_output":{"file":{"content":"\"\"\"Episodic Store — records every decision outcome for the learning loop.\"\"\"\nimport json\nimport time\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom typing import Any\nfrom uuid import uuid4\n\nimport aiosqlite\n\n\nclass EpisodicStore:\n    def __init__(self, db_path: Path) -> None:\n        self._db = db_path\n\n    async def create_episode(\n        self,\n        decision_id: str,\n        intent_class: str,\n        action_type: str,\n        entity_class: str,\n        actor_role: str,\n        context_snapshot: dict[str, Any],\n        generation_path: str = \"MODEL\",\n    ) -> str:\n        episode_id = str(uuid4())\n        async with aiosqlite.connect(self._db) as db:\n            await db.execute(\n                \"\"\"INSERT INTO episodes\n                   (episode_id, decision_id, intent_class, action_type, entity_class,\n                    actor_role, context_snapshot, generation_path, created_at)\n                   VALUES (?, ?, ?, ?, ?, ?, ?, ?, ?)\"\"\",\n                (episode_id, decision_id, intent_class, action_type, entity_class,\n                 actor_role, json.dumps(context_snapshot), generation_path, time.time()),\n            )\n            await db.commit()\n        return episode_id\n\n    async def complete_episode(\n        self,\n        decision_id: str,\n        outcome: str,\n        observed_state_delta: dict[str, Any],\n        side_effects: list[str],\n        duration_ms: int,\n        anomalies: list[str],\n    ) -> str | None:\n        snapshot = {\n            \"observed_state_delta\": observed_state_delta,\n            \"side_effects_observed\": side_effects,\n            \"duration_ms\": duration_ms,\n            \"anomalies\": anomalies,\n        }\n        async with aiosqlite.connect(self._db) as db:\n            async with db.execute(\n                \"SELECT episode_id FROM episodes WHERE decision_id = ?\", (decision_id,)\n            ) as cursor:\n                row = await cursor.fetchone()\n            if not row:\n                return None\n            episode_id = row[0]\n            await db.execute(\n                \"\"\"UPDATE episodes SET outcome = ?, context_snapshot = json_patch(context_snapshot, ?),\n                   completed_at = ? WHERE episode_id = ?\"\"\",\n                (outcome, json.dumps(snapshot), time.time(), episode_id),\n            )\n            await db.commit()\n        return episode_id\n\n    async def write_prediction_update(\n        self,\n        episode_id: str,\n        prediction_delta: float,\n        early_reextraction_flag: bool,\n    ) -> None:\n        async with aiosqlite.connect(self._db) as db:\n            await db.execute(\n                \"\"\"UPDATE episodes SET prediction_delta = ?, early_reextraction_flag = ?\n                   WHERE episode_id = ?\"\"\",\n                (prediction_delta, int(early_reextraction_flag), episode_id),\n            )\n            await db.commit()\n\n    async def fetch_for_extraction(\n        self,\n        intent_class: str,\n        action_type: str,\n        entity_class: str,\n        actor_role: str,\n        limit: int = 500,\n    ) -> list[dict[str, Any]]:\n        \"\"\"Fetch completed, non-rule-based episodes for a given context tuple.\"\"\"\n        async with aiosqlite.connect(self._db) as db:\n            db.row_factory = aiosqlite.Row\n            async with db.execute(\n                \"\"\"SELECT episode_id, outcome, prediction_delta\n                   FROM episodes\n                   WHERE intent_class = ? AND action_type = ? AND entity_class = ?\n                     AND actor_role = ? AND outcome IS NOT NULL\n                     AND generation_path = 'MODEL'\n                   ORDER BY created_at DESC LIMIT ?\"\"\",\n                (intent_class, action_type, entity_class, actor_role, limit),\n            ) as cursor:\n                rows = await cursor.fetchall()\n        return [dict(r) for r in rows]\n\n    async def fetch_for_manifest(\n        self,\n        intent_class: str,\n        entity_class: str,\n        actor_role: str,\n        lookback_days: int = 30,\n        max_episodes: int = 20,\n    ) -> list[dict[str, Any]]:\n        cutoff = time.time() - lookback_days * 86400\n        async with aiosqlite.connect(self._db) as db:\n            db.row_factory = aiosqlite.Row\n            async with db.execute(\n                \"\"\"SELECT episode_id, action_type, entity_class, outcome, created_at\n                   FROM episodes\n                   WHERE intent_class = ? AND entity_class = ? AND actor_role = ?\n                     AND created_at >= ? AND outcome IS NOT NULL\n                   ORDER BY created_at DESC LIMIT ?\"\"\",\n                (intent_class, entity_class, actor_role, cutoff, max_episodes),\n            ) as cursor:\n                rows = await cursor.fetchall()\n        return [dict(r) for r in rows]\n\n    async def get_distinct_tuples(self) -> list[tuple[str, str, str, str]]:\n        \"\"\"All (intent_class, action_type, entity_class, actor_role) tuples with completed episodes.\"\"\"\n        async with aiosqlite.connect(self._db) as db:\n            async with db.execute(\n                \"\"\"SELECT DISTINCT intent_class, action_type, entity_class, actor_role\n                   FROM episodes WHERE outcome IS NOT NULL\"\"\"\n            ) as cursor:\n                rows = await cursor.fetchall()\n        return [tuple(r) for r in rows]\n\n    async def get_flagged_for_early_extraction(self) -> list[tuple[str, str, str, str]]:\n        async with aiosqlite.connect(self._db) as db:\n            async with db.execute(\n                \"\"\"SELECT DISTINCT intent_class, action_type, entity_class, actor_role\n                   FROM episodes WHERE early_reextraction_flag = 1 AND outcome IS NOT NULL\"\"\"\n            ) as cursor:\n                rows = await cursor.fetchall()\n        return [tuple(r) for r in rows]\n\n    async def clear_early_extraction_flags(self) -> None:\n        async with aiosqlite.connect(self._db) as db:\n            await db.execute(\"UPDATE episodes SET early_reextraction_flag = 0\")\n            await db.commit()\n","filePath":"/Users/xnch/xnchSystems/xnch/xnch/memory/episodic_store.py","numLines":151,"startLine":1,"totalLines":151},"type":"text"}},"sessionId":"283b9ba1-0eba-4a0c-ba9d-0cf00eb4bc4b","timestamp":"2026-06-26T17:28:35.699Z","toolInput":{"file_path":"/Users/xnch/xnchSystems/xnch/xnch/memory/episodic_store.py"},"toolName":"Read","toolOutput":{"file":{"content":"\"\"\"Episodic Store — records every decision outcome for the learning loop.\"\"\"\nimport json\nimport time\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom typing import Any\nfrom uuid import uuid4\n\nimport aiosqlite\n\n\nclass EpisodicStore:\n    def __init__(self, db_path: Path) -> None:\n        self._db = db_path\n\n    async def create_episode(\n        self,\n        decision_id: str,\n        intent_class: str,\n        action_type: str,\n        entity_class: str,\n        actor_role: str,\n        context_snapshot: dict[str, Any],\n        generation_path: str = \"MODEL\",\n    ) -> str:\n        episode_id = str(uuid4())\n        async with aiosqlite.connect(self._db) as db:\n            await db.execute(\n                \"\"\"INSERT INTO episodes\n                   (episode_id, decision_id, intent_class, action_type, entity_class,\n                    actor_role, context_snapshot, generation_path, created_at)\n                   VALUES (?, ?, ?, ?, ?, ?, ?, ?, ?)\"\"\",\n                (episode_id, decision_id, intent_class, action_type, entity_class,\n                 actor_role, json.dumps(context_snapshot), generation_path, time.time()),\n            )\n            await db.commit()\n        return episode_id\n\n    async def complete_episode(\n        self,\n        decision_id: str,\n        outcome: str,\n        observed_state_delta: dict[str, Any],\n        side_effects: list[str],\n        duration_ms: int,\n        anomalies: list[str],\n    ) -> str | None:\n        snapshot = {\n            \"observed_state_delta\": observed_state_delta,\n            \"side_effects_observed\": side_effects,\n            \"duration_ms\": duration_ms,\n            \"anomalies\": anomalies,\n        }\n        async with aiosqlite.connect(self._db) as db:\n            async with db.execute(\n                \"SELECT episode_id FROM episodes WHERE decision_id = ?\", (decision_id,)\n            ) as cursor:\n                row = await cursor.fetchone()\n            if not row:\n                return None\n            episode_id = row[0]\n            await db.execute(\n                \"\"\"UPDATE episodes SET outcome = ?, context_snapshot = json_patch(context_snapshot, ?),\n                   completed_at = ? WHERE episode_id = ?\"\"\",\n                (outcome, json.dumps(snapshot), time.time(), episode_id),\n            )\n            await db.commit()\n        return episode_id\n\n    async def write_prediction_update(\n        self,\n        episode_id: str,\n        prediction_delta: float,\n        early_reextraction_flag: bool,\n    ) -> None:\n        async with aiosqlite.connect(self._db) as db:\n            await db.execute(\n                \"\"\"UPDATE episodes SET prediction_delta = ?, early_reextraction_flag = ?\n                   WHERE episode_id = ?\"\"\",\n                (prediction_delta, int(early_reextraction_flag), episode_id),\n            )\n            await db.commit()\n\n    async def fetch_for_extraction(\n        self,\n        intent_class: str,\n        action_type: str,\n        entity_class: str,\n        actor_role: str,\n        limit: int = 500,\n    ) -> list[dict[str, Any]]:\n        \"\"\"Fetch completed, non-rule-based episodes for a given context tuple.\"\"\"\n        async with aiosqlite.connect(self._db) as db:\n            db.row_factory = aiosqlite.Row\n            async with db.execute(\n                \"\"\"SELECT episode_id, outcome, prediction_delta\n                   FROM episodes\n                   WHERE intent_class = ? AND action_type = ? AND entity_class = ?\n                     AND actor_role = ? AND outcome IS NOT NULL\n                     AND generation_path = 'MODEL'\n                   ORDER BY created_at DESC LIMIT ?\"\"\",\n                (intent_class, action_type, entity_class, actor_role, limit),\n            ) as cursor:\n                rows = await cursor.fetchall()\n        return [dict(r) for r in rows]\n\n    async def fetch_for_manifest(\n        self,\n        intent_class: str,\n        entity_class: str,\n        actor_role: str,\n        lookback_days: int = 30,\n        max_episodes: int = 20,\n    ) -> list[dict[str, Any]]:\n        cutoff = time.time() - lookback_days * 86400\n        async with aiosqlite.connect(self._db) as db:\n            db.row_factory = aiosqlite.Row\n            async with db.execute(\n                \"\"\"SELECT episode_id, action_type, entity_class, outcome, created_at\n                   FROM episodes\n                   WHERE intent_class = ? AND entity_class = ? AND actor_role = ?\n                     AND created_at >= ? AND outcome IS NOT NULL\n                   ORDER BY created_at DESC LIMIT ?\"\"\",\n                (intent_class, entity_class, actor_role, cutoff, max_episodes),\n            ) as cursor:\n                rows = await cursor.fetchall()\n        return [dict(r) for r in rows]\n\n    async def get_distinct_tuples(self) -> list[tuple[str, str, str, str]]:\n        \"\"\"All (intent_class, action_type, entity_class, actor_role) tuples with completed episodes.\"\"\"\n        async with aiosqlite.connect(self._db) as db:\n            async with db.execute(\n                \"\"\"SELECT DISTINCT intent_class, action_type, entity_class, actor_role\n                   FROM episodes WHERE outcome IS NOT NULL\"\"\"\n            ) as cursor:\n                rows = await cursor.fetchall()\n        return [tuple(r) for r in rows]\n\n    async def get_flagged_for_early_extraction(self) -> list[tuple[str, str, str, str]]:\n        async with aiosqlite.connect(self._db) as db:\n            async with db.execute(\n                \"\"\"SELECT DISTINCT intent_class, action_type, entity_class, actor_role\n                   FROM episodes WHERE early_reextraction_flag = 1 AND outcome IS NOT NULL\"\"\"\n            ) as cursor:\n                rows = await cursor.fetchall()\n        return [tuple(r) for r in rows]\n\n    async def clear_early_extraction_flags(self) -> None:\n        async with aiosqlite.connect(self._db) as db:\n            await db.execute(\"UPDATE episodes SET early_reextraction_flag = 0\")\n            await db.commit()\n","filePath":"/Users/xnch/xnchSystems/xnch/xnch/memory/episodic_store.py","numLines":151,"startLine":1,"totalLines":151},"type":"text"}},"type":"raw"},"obs_mqv7gfpz_587dc9e4d449":{"observation":{"hookType":"post_tool_use","id":"obs_mqv7gfpz_587dc9e4d449","raw":{"tool_input":{"file_path":"/Users/xnch/xnchSystems/nexi/nexi/pipeline/context_assembler.py"},"tool_name":"Read","tool_output":{"file":{"content":"from __future__ import annotations\n\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass, field\nfrom datetime import datetime, timezone\nfrom typing import Any\n\nfrom nexi.character.prompt_loader import build_system_prompt\n\n\n@dataclass\nclass AssembledContext:\n    system_prompt: str = \"\"\n    recent_turns: list[dict] = field(default_factory=list)\n    relevant_episodes: list[str] = field(default_factory=list)\n    entity_context: list[dict] = field(default_factory=list)\n    relationship_context: list[dict] = field(default_factory=list)\n    perception_snippets: list[str] = field(default_factory=list)\n\n    def to_messages(self, raw_input: str) -> list[dict]:\n        msgs = [{\"role\": \"system\", \"content\": self.system_prompt}]\n        for t in self.recent_turns:\n            msgs.append({\"role\": t.get(\"role\", \"user\"), \"content\": t.get(\"content\", \"\")})\n        msgs.append({\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": raw_input})\n        return msgs\n\n\ndef _extract_entity_mentions(text: str) -> list[str]:\n    import re\n    matches = re.findall(r'\\b([A-Z][a-z]+(?: [A-Z][a-z]+)*)\\b', text)\n    seen = set()\n    entities = []\n    for m in matches:\n        if m.lower() not in seen and len(m) > 2:\n            seen.add(m.lower())\n            entities.append(m)\n    return entities\n\n\nasync def assemble_context(\n    session_id: str,\n    raw_input: str,\n    working_memory,\n    pg_episodic,\n    graph_store,\n    relationship_store,\n    sensory_buffer,\n    proactivity_engine=None,\n) -> AssembledContext:\n    ctx = AssembledContext()\n\n    recent_turns = await working_memory.get_turns(session_id, last_n=20)\n    ctx.recent_turns = recent_turns\n\n    relevant = await pg_episodic.retrieve_similar(\n        query_text=raw_input, top_k=5\n    )\n    ctx.relevant_episodes = [\n        r.get(\"summary\") or r.get(\"raw_text\", \"\") for r in relevant\n    ]\n\n    entities = _extract_entity_mentions(raw_input)\n    if entities:\n        for ent in entities:\n            entity_node = graph_store.get_entity_by_name(ent)\n            if entity_node:\n                eid = entity_node[\"metadata\"].get(\"entity_id\", ent)\n                connections = graph_store.query_entity_connections(eid)\n                ctx.entity_context.extend(connections)\n                rels = await relationship_store.get_relationships(eid)\n                ctx.relationship_context.extend(\n                    {\"entity_a\": r.entity_a_id, \"entity_b\": r.entity_b_id,\n                     \"type\": r.relationship_type, \"strength\": r.strength}\n                    for r in rels\n                )\n\n    recent_perceptions = await sensory_buffer.read_recent(\"voice\", limit=3)\n    ctx.perception_snippets = [p.get(\"data\", \"\") for p in recent_perceptions]\n\n    session_memories = ctx.relevant_episodes[:5]\n    session_entities = [f\"{c.get('connected_name', '')} ({c.get('rel_type', '')})\" for c in ctx.entity_context[:5]]\n    ctx.system_prompt = build_system_prompt(\n        session_memory=[{\"summary\": s} for s in session_memories],\n        recent_entities=session_entities,\n    )\n\n    if proactivity_engine is not None:\n        pending = await proactivity_engine.get_pending()\n        if pending:\n            obs_lines = \"\\n\".join(e.message for e in pending)\n            ctx.system_prompt += f\"\\n\\n## Pending Observations\\n{obs_lines}\"\n\n    ts = datetime.now(timezone.utc).isoformat()\n    ctx.system_prompt += f\"\\n\\nContext assembled at {ts}\"\n\n    return ctx\n","filePath":"/Users/xnch/xnchSystems/nexi/nexi/pipeline/context_assembler.py","numLines":96,"startLine":1,"totalLines":96},"type":"text"}},"sessionId":"283b9ba1-0eba-4a0c-ba9d-0cf00eb4bc4b","timestamp":"2026-06-26T17:28:46.440Z","toolInput":{"file_path":"/Users/xnch/xnchSystems/nexi/nexi/pipeline/context_assembler.py"},"toolName":"Read","toolOutput":{"file":{"content":"from __future__ import annotations\n\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass, field\nfrom datetime import datetime, timezone\nfrom typing import Any\n\nfrom nexi.character.prompt_loader import build_system_prompt\n\n\n@dataclass\nclass AssembledContext:\n    system_prompt: str = \"\"\n    recent_turns: list[dict] = field(default_factory=list)\n    relevant_episodes: list[str] = field(default_factory=list)\n    entity_context: list[dict] = field(default_factory=list)\n    relationship_context: list[dict] = field(default_factory=list)\n    perception_snippets: list[str] = field(default_factory=list)\n\n    def to_messages(self, raw_input: str) -> list[dict]:\n        msgs = [{\"role\": \"system\", \"content\": self.system_prompt}]\n        for t in self.recent_turns:\n            msgs.append({\"role\": t.get(\"role\", \"user\"), \"content\": t.get(\"content\", \"\")})\n        msgs.append({\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": raw_input})\n        return msgs\n\n\ndef _extract_entity_mentions(text: str) -> list[str]:\n    import re\n    matches = re.findall(r'\\b([A-Z][a-z]+(?: [A-Z][a-z]+)*)\\b', text)\n    seen = set()\n    entities = []\n    for m in matches:\n        if m.lower() not in seen and len(m) > 2:\n            seen.add(m.lower())\n            entities.append(m)\n    return entities\n\n\nasync def assemble_context(\n    session_id: str,\n    raw_input: str,\n    working_memory,\n    pg_episodic,\n    graph_store,\n    relationship_store,\n    sensory_buffer,\n    proactivity_engine=None,\n) -> AssembledContext:\n    ctx = AssembledContext()\n\n    recent_turns = await working_memory.get_turns(session_id, last_n=20)\n    ctx.recent_turns = recent_turns\n\n    relevant = await pg_episodic.retrieve_similar(\n        query_text=raw_input, top_k=5\n    )\n    ctx.relevant_episodes = [\n        r.get(\"summary\") or r.get(\"raw_text\", \"\") for r in relevant\n    ]\n\n    entities = _extract_entity_mentions(raw_input)\n    if entities:\n        for ent in entities:\n            entity_node = graph_store.get_entity_by_name(ent)\n            if entity_node:\n                eid = entity_node[\"metadata\"].get(\"entity_id\", ent)\n                connections = graph_store.query_entity_connections(eid)\n                ctx.entity_context.extend(connections)\n                rels = await relationship_store.get_relationships(eid)\n                ctx.relationship_context.extend(\n                    {\"entity_a\": r.entity_a_id, \"entity_b\": r.entity_b_id,\n                     \"type\": r.relationship_type, \"strength\": r.strength}\n                    for r in rels\n                )\n\n    recent_perceptions = await sensory_buffer.read_recent(\"voice\", limit=3)\n    ctx.perception_snippets = [p.get(\"data\", \"\") for p in recent_perceptions]\n\n    session_memories = ctx.relevant_episodes[:5]\n    session_entities = [f\"{c.get('connected_name', '')} ({c.get('rel_type', '')})\" for c in ctx.entity_context[:5]]\n    ctx.system_prompt = build_system_prompt(\n        session_memory=[{\"summary\": s} for s in session_memories],\n        recent_entities=session_entities,\n    )\n\n    if proactivity_engine is not None:\n        pending = await proactivity_engine.get_pending()\n        if pending:\n            obs_lines = \"\\n\".join(e.message for e in pending)\n            ctx.system_prompt += f\"\\n\\n## Pending Observations\\n{obs_lines}\"\n\n    ts = datetime.now(timezone.utc).isoformat()\n    ctx.system_prompt += f\"\\n\\nContext assembled at {ts}\"\n\n    return ctx\n","filePath":"/Users/xnch/xnchSystems/nexi/nexi/pipeline/context_assembler.py","numLines":96,"startLine":1,"totalLines":96},"type":"text"}},"type":"raw"},"obs_mqv7gg33_202cb6e91313":{"observation":{"hookType":"post_tool_use","id":"obs_mqv7gg33_202cb6e91313","raw":{"tool_input":{"file_path":"/Users/xnch/xnchSystems/nexi/nexi/pipeline/intent_interpreter.py"},"tool_name":"Read","tool_output":"{\"type\":\"text\",\"file\":{\"filePath\":\"/Users/xnch/xnchSystems/nexi/nexi/pipeline/intent_interpreter.py\",\"content\":\"\\\"\\\"\\\"Step 3 — Intent Normalization (Contract 4). LiteLLM-backed classifier.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\nimport hashlib\\nimport json\\nimport re\\nfrom typing import Any\\nfrom uuid import UUID\\n\\nimport httpx\\nfrom agentmemory import create_memory, search_memory\\n\\nfrom ..config import settings\\nfrom ..models.intent import Intent, IntentClass, ActionType, Urgency\\nfrom ..utils.audit import emit_event\\nfrom xnch.security.injection_guard import scan_input, InjectionResult\\n\\n\\nclass PolicyViolation(Exception):\\n    pass\\n\\n\\n_CLASSIFICATION_SYSTEM_PROMPT = \\\"\\\"\\\"You are an intent classifier for a systems-management agent.\\nClassify the user's raw input into one of these intent classes:\\n\\n- QUERY: Read-only information retrieval (list, show, get, fetch, display)\\n- DECISION: Planning, design, recommendation, analysis for decision support\\n- EXECUTION: Mutating actions (deploy, rollback, write, delete, backup, run)\\n- ESCALATION: Escalate to human operator\\n\\nRespond with a JSON object using this schema:\\n{\\n  \\\"intent_class\\\": \\\"QUERY|DECISION|EXECUTION|ESCALATION\\\",\\n  \\\"action_type\\\": \\\"<appropriate action from the list below>\\\",\\n  \\\"entity_class\\\": \\\"<guessed entity type: ML_MODEL|SERVICE|DATABASE|CLUSTER|FILE|SCRIPT|SCHEMA|RESOURCE>\\\",\\n  \\\"urgency\\\": \\\"LOW|NORMAL|HIGH|CRITICAL\\\",\\n  \\\"entity_id\\\": \\\"<the noun phrase identifying the target>\\\",\\n  \\\"clarifications_needed\\\": [\\\"<question if ambiguous>\\\"]\\n}\\n\\nAction types by class:\\nQUERY → READ_FILE, LIST, ANALYZE, QUERY\\nDECISION → PLAN, ANALYZE\\nEXECUTION → DEPLOY, ROLLBACK, BACKUP, RESTORE, WRITE_FILE, DELETE_FILE, RUN_COMMAND, RUN_SCRIPT, STAGE, MUTATE\\nESCALATION → ESCALATE\\n\\nIf the input is ambiguous (multiple interpretations possible), populates clarifications_needed\\nwith specific questions to disambiguate. Otherwise leave it empty.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\n\\nclass ClarificationRequired(Exception):\\n    def __init__(self, session_id: UUID, ambiguity_score: float, questions: list[str] | None = None) -> None:\\n        self.session_id = session_id\\n        self.ambiguity_score = ambiguity_score\\n        self.questions = questions or []\\n        msg = f\\\"Ambiguity score {ambiguity_score:.2f} exceeds threshold\\\"\\n        if self.questions:\\n            msg += f\\\"; questions: {'; '.join(self.questions)}\\\"\\n        super().__init__(msg)\\n\\n\\n# Stage 1: rule-based pre-filter (confidence=1.0, ambiguity=0.0)\\n_RULES: list[tuple[re.Pattern, IntentClass, str]] = [\\n    (re.compile(r\\\"^(list|show all|enumerate)\\\\b\\\", re.I), IntentClass.QUERY, \\\"LIST\\\"),\\n    (re.compile(r\\\"^(show|read|get|fetch|display)\\\\b\\\", re.I), IntentClass.QUERY, \\\"READ_FILE\\\"),\\n    (re.compile(r\\\"^(analyze|inspect|check|scan)\\\\b\\\", re.I), IntentClass.QUERY, \\\"ANALYZE\\\"),\\n    (re.compile(r\\\"^(deploy|launch|start|spin up)\\\\b\\\", re.I), IntentClass.EXECUTION, \\\"DEPLOY\\\"),\\n    (re.compile(r\\\"^(rollback|revert)\\\\b\\\", re.I), IntentClass.EXECUTION, \\\"ROLLBACK\\\"),\\n    (re.compile(r\\\"^back(up|fill)\\\\b\\\", re.I), IntentClass.EXECUTION, \\\"BACKUP\\\"),\\n    (re.compile(r\\\"^(delete|remove|drop)\\\\b\\\", re.I), IntentClass.EXECUTION, \\\"DELETE_FILE\\\"),\\n    (re.compile(r\\\"^(write|create|add)\\\\b\\\", re.I), IntentClass.EXECUTION, \\\"WRITE_FILE\\\"),\\n    (re.compile(r\\\"^(plan|design|propose)\\\\b\\\", re.I), IntentClass.DECISION, \\\"PLAN\\\"),\\n    (re.compile(r\\\"^(recommend|suggest|advise)\\\\b\\\", re.I), IntentClass.DECISION, \\\"ANALYZE\\\"),\\n    (re.compile(r\\\"^escalate\\\\b\\\", re.I), IntentClass.ESCALATION, \\\"ESCALATE\\\"),\\n]\\n\\n\\ndef _rule_classify(raw_input: str) -> tuple[IntentClass, str, float, float] | None:\\n    for pattern, intent_class, action_type in _RULES:\\n        if pattern.search(raw_input.strip()):\\n            return intent_class, action_type, 1.0, 0.0\\n    return None\\n\\n\\ndef _extract_entity(raw_input: str) -> tuple[str, str]:\\n    tokens = raw_input.strip().split()\\n    entity_id = tokens[1] if len(tokens) > 1 else \\\"unknown\\\"\\n    entity_class_hints = {\\n        \\\"model\\\": \\\"ML_MODEL\\\", \\\"service\\\": \\\"SERVICE\\\", \\\"db\\\": \\\"DATABASE\\\",\\n        \\\"database\\\": \\\"DATABASE\\\", \\\"cluster\\\": \\\"CLUSTER\\\", \\\"file\\\": \\\"FILE\\\",\\n        \\\"script\\\": \\\"SCRIPT\\\", \\\"schema\\\": \\\"SCHEMA\\\",\\n    }\\n    for token in tokens:\\n        for hint, cls in entity_class_hints.items():\\n            if hint in token.lower():\\n                return entity_id, cls\\n    return entity_id, \\\"RESOURCE\\\"\\n\\n\\ndef _recall_intent(raw_input: str) -> Intent | None:\\n    try:\\n        results = search_memory(\\\"intent-classifications\\\", raw_input, n_results=3, include_embeddings=False)\\n        for item in results:\\n            mem = item.get(\\\"document\\\", \\\"\\\") if isinstance(item, dict) else str(item)\\n            if isinstance(mem, str):\\n                try:\\n                    data = json.loads(mem)\\n                    if data.get(\\\"raw_input\\\", \\\"\\\").lower().strip() == raw_input.lower().strip():\\n                        return Intent(\\n                            session_id=UUID(int=0),\\n                            intent_class=IntentClass(data[\\\"intent_class\\\"]),\\n                            action_type=ActionType(data[\\\"action_type\\\"]),\\n                            target_entity_id=data.get(\\\"entity_id\\\", \\\"unknown\\\"),\\n                            target_entity_class=data.get(\\\"entity_class\\\", \\\"RESOURCE\\\"),\\n                            urgency=Urgency(data.get(\\\"urgency\\\", \\\"NORMAL\\\")),\\n                            ambiguity_score=0.0,\\n                            raw_input_hash=\\\"\\\",\\n                            raw_input=raw_input,\\n                        )\\n                except Exception:\\n                    pass\\n    except Exception:\\n        pass\\n    return None\\n\\n\\ndef _persist_intent(raw_input: str, intent: Intent) -> None:\\n    try:\\n        create_memory(\\n            \\\"intent-classifications\\\",\\n            json.dumps({\\n                \\\"raw_input\\\": raw_input,\\n                \\\"intent_class\\\": intent.intent_class,\\n                \\\"action_type\\\": intent.action_type,\\n                \\\"entity_id\\\": intent.target_entity_id,\\n                \\\"entity_class\\\": intent.target_entity_class,\\n                \\\"urgency\\\": intent.urgency,\\n            }),\\n            metadata={\\n                \\\"intent_class\\\": intent.intent_class,\\n                \\\"action_type\\\": intent.action_type,\\n            },\\n        )\\n    except Exception:\\n        pass\\n\\n\\nclass IntentInterpreter:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Contract 4 two-stage classifier: rule-based pre-filter + LiteLLM fallback.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\n    async def interpret(self, raw_input: str, session_id: UUID, trace_id: str) -> Intent:\\n        raw_input_hash = \\\"sha256:\\\" + hashlib.sha256(raw_input.encode()).hexdigest()\\n\\n        injection_result = scan_input(raw_input)\\n        if not injection_result.is_clean:\\n            emit_event(trace_id, \\\"intent_interpreter\\\", \\\"INJECTION_BLOCKED\\\",\\n                       {\\\"risk_score\\\": injection_result.risk_score,\\n                        \\\"matched_patterns\\\": injection_result.matched_patterns})\\n            raise PolicyViolation(f\\\"Input failed injection scan (risk={injection_result.risk_score:.2f})\\\")\\n\\n        emit_event(trace_id, \\\"intent_interpreter\\\", \\\"CLASSIFY_START\\\")\\n\\n        rule_result = _rule_classify(raw_input)\\n        if rule_result:\\n            intent_class, action_type, confidence, ambiguity_score = rule_result\\n            classification_method = \\\"rule\\\"\\n\\n            if ambiguity_score > 0.7:\\n                emit_event(trace_id, \\\"intent_interpreter\\\", \\\"CLARIFICATION_REQUIRED\\\",\\n                           {\\\"ambiguity_score\\\": ambiguity_score})\\n                raise ClarificationRequired(session_id, ambiguity_score)\\n\\n            entity_id, entity_class = _extract_entity(raw_input)\\n            intent = Intent(\\n                session_id=session_id,\\n                intent_class=intent_class,\\n                action_type=ActionType(action_type),\\n                target_entity_id=entity_i...[truncated]"},"sessionId":"283b9ba1-0eba-4a0c-ba9d-0cf00eb4bc4b","timestamp":"2026-06-26T17:28:46.913Z","toolInput":{"file_path":"/Users/xnch/xnchSystems/nexi/nexi/pipeline/intent_interpreter.py"},"toolName":"Read","toolOutput":"{\"type\":\"text\",\"file\":{\"filePath\":\"/Users/xnch/xnchSystems/nexi/nexi/pipeline/intent_interpreter.py\",\"content\":\"\\\"\\\"\\\"Step 3 — Intent Normalization (Contract 4). LiteLLM-backed classifier.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\nimport hashlib\\nimport json\\nimport re\\nfrom typing import Any\\nfrom uuid import UUID\\n\\nimport httpx\\nfrom agentmemory import create_memory, search_memory\\n\\nfrom ..config import settings\\nfrom ..models.intent import Intent, IntentClass, ActionType, Urgency\\nfrom ..utils.audit import emit_event\\nfrom xnch.security.injection_guard import scan_input, InjectionResult\\n\\n\\nclass PolicyViolation(Exception):\\n    pass\\n\\n\\n_CLASSIFICATION_SYSTEM_PROMPT = \\\"\\\"\\\"You are an intent classifier for a systems-management agent.\\nClassify the user's raw input into one of these intent classes:\\n\\n- QUERY: Read-only information retrieval (list, show, get, fetch, display)\\n- DECISION: Planning, design, recommendation, analysis for decision support\\n- EXECUTION: Mutating actions (deploy, rollback, write, delete, backup, run)\\n- ESCALATION: Escalate to human operator\\n\\nRespond with a JSON object using this schema:\\n{\\n  \\\"intent_class\\\": \\\"QUERY|DECISION|EXECUTION|ESCALATION\\\",\\n  \\\"action_type\\\": \\\"<appropriate action from the list below>\\\",\\n  \\\"entity_class\\\": \\\"<guessed entity type: ML_MODEL|SERVICE|DATABASE|CLUSTER|FILE|SCRIPT|SCHEMA|RESOURCE>\\\",\\n  \\\"urgency\\\": \\\"LOW|NORMAL|HIGH|CRITICAL\\\",\\n  \\\"entity_id\\\": \\\"<the noun phrase identifying the target>\\\",\\n  \\\"clarifications_needed\\\": [\\\"<question if ambiguous>\\\"]\\n}\\n\\nAction types by class:\\nQUERY → READ_FILE, LIST, ANALYZE, QUERY\\nDECISION → PLAN, ANALYZE\\nEXECUTION → DEPLOY, ROLLBACK, BACKUP, RESTORE, WRITE_FILE, DELETE_FILE, RUN_COMMAND, RUN_SCRIPT, STAGE, MUTATE\\nESCALATION → ESCALATE\\n\\nIf the input is ambiguous (multiple interpretations possible), populates clarifications_needed\\nwith specific questions to disambiguate. Otherwise leave it empty.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\n\\nclass ClarificationRequired(Exception):\\n    def __init__(self, session_id: UUID, ambiguity_score: float, questions: list[str] | None = None) -> None:\\n        self.session_id = session_id\\n        self.ambiguity_score = ambiguity_score\\n        self.questions = questions or []\\n        msg = f\\\"Ambiguity score {ambiguity_score:.2f} exceeds threshold\\\"\\n        if self.questions:\\n            msg += f\\\"; questions: {'; '.join(self.questions)}\\\"\\n        super().__init__(msg)\\n\\n\\n# Stage 1: rule-based pre-filter (confidence=1.0, ambiguity=0.0)\\n_RULES: list[tuple[re.Pattern, IntentClass, str]] = [\\n    (re.compile(r\\\"^(list|show all|enumerate)\\\\b\\\", re.I), IntentClass.QUERY, \\\"LIST\\\"),\\n    (re.compile(r\\\"^(show|read|get|fetch|display)\\\\b\\\", re.I), IntentClass.QUERY, \\\"READ_FILE\\\"),\\n    (re.compile(r\\\"^(analyze|inspect|check|scan)\\\\b\\\", re.I), IntentClass.QUERY, \\\"ANALYZE\\\"),\\n    (re.compile(r\\\"^(deploy|launch|start|spin up)\\\\b\\\", re.I), IntentClass.EXECUTION, \\\"DEPLOY\\\"),\\n    (re.compile(r\\\"^(rollback|revert)\\\\b\\\", re.I), IntentClass.EXECUTION, \\\"ROLLBACK\\\"),\\n    (re.compile(r\\\"^back(up|fill)\\\\b\\\", re.I), IntentClass.EXECUTION, \\\"BACKUP\\\"),\\n    (re.compile(r\\\"^(delete|remove|drop)\\\\b\\\", re.I), IntentClass.EXECUTION, \\\"DELETE_FILE\\\"),\\n    (re.compile(r\\\"^(write|create|add)\\\\b\\\", re.I), IntentClass.EXECUTION, \\\"WRITE_FILE\\\"),\\n    (re.compile(r\\\"^(plan|design|propose)\\\\b\\\", re.I), IntentClass.DECISION, \\\"PLAN\\\"),\\n    (re.compile(r\\\"^(recommend|suggest|advise)\\\\b\\\", re.I), IntentClass.DECISION, \\\"ANALYZE\\\"),\\n    (re.compile(r\\\"^escalate\\\\b\\\", re.I), IntentClass.ESCALATION, \\\"ESCALATE\\\"),\\n]\\n\\n\\ndef _rule_classify(raw_input: str) -> tuple[IntentClass, str, float, float] | None:\\n    for pattern, intent_class, action_type in _RULES:\\n        if pattern.search(raw_input.strip()):\\n            return intent_class, action_type, 1.0, 0.0\\n    return None\\n\\n\\ndef _extract_entity(raw_input: str) -> tuple[str, str]:\\n    tokens = raw_input.strip().split()\\n    entity_id = tokens[1] if len(tokens) > 1 else \\\"unknown\\\"\\n    entity_class_hints = {\\n        \\\"model\\\": \\\"ML_MODEL\\\", \\\"service\\\": \\\"SERVICE\\\", \\\"db\\\": \\\"DATABASE\\\",\\n        \\\"database\\\": \\\"DATABASE\\\", \\\"cluster\\\": \\\"CLUSTER\\\", \\\"file\\\": \\\"FILE\\\",\\n        \\\"script\\\": \\\"SCRIPT\\\", \\\"schema\\\": \\\"SCHEMA\\\",\\n    }\\n    for token in tokens:\\n        for hint, cls in entity_class_hints.items():\\n            if hint in token.lower():\\n                return entity_id, cls\\n    return entity_id, \\\"RESOURCE\\\"\\n\\n\\ndef _recall_intent(raw_input: str) -> Intent | None:\\n    try:\\n        results = search_memory(\\\"intent-classifications\\\", raw_input, n_results=3, include_embeddings=False)\\n        for item in results:\\n            mem = item.get(\\\"document\\\", \\\"\\\") if isinstance(item, dict) else str(item)\\n            if isinstance(mem, str):\\n                try:\\n                    data = json.loads(mem)\\n                    if data.get(\\\"raw_input\\\", \\\"\\\").lower().strip() == raw_input.lower().strip():\\n                        return Intent(\\n                            session_id=UUID(int=0),\\n                            intent_class=IntentClass(data[\\\"intent_class\\\"]),\\n                            action_type=ActionType(data[\\\"action_type\\\"]),\\n                            target_entity_id=data.get(\\\"entity_id\\\", \\\"unknown\\\"),\\n                            target_entity_class=data.get(\\\"entity_class\\\", \\\"RESOURCE\\\"),\\n                            urgency=Urgency(data.get(\\\"urgency\\\", \\\"NORMAL\\\")),\\n                            ambiguity_score=0.0,\\n                            raw_input_hash=\\\"\\\",\\n                            raw_input=raw_input,\\n                        )\\n                except Exception:\\n                    pass\\n    except Exception:\\n        pass\\n    return None\\n\\n\\ndef _persist_intent(raw_input: str, intent: Intent) -> None:\\n    try:\\n        create_memory(\\n            \\\"intent-classifications\\\",\\n            json.dumps({\\n                \\\"raw_input\\\": raw_input,\\n                \\\"intent_class\\\": intent.intent_class,\\n                \\\"action_type\\\": intent.action_type,\\n                \\\"entity_id\\\": intent.target_entity_id,\\n                \\\"entity_class\\\": intent.target_entity_class,\\n                \\\"urgency\\\": intent.urgency,\\n            }),\\n            metadata={\\n                \\\"intent_class\\\": intent.intent_class,\\n                \\\"action_type\\\": intent.action_type,\\n            },\\n        )\\n    except Exception:\\n        pass\\n\\n\\nclass IntentInterpreter:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Contract 4 two-stage classifier: rule-based pre-filter + LiteLLM fallback.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\n    async def interpret(self, raw_input: str, session_id: UUID, trace_id: str) -> Intent:\\n        raw_input_hash = \\\"sha256:\\\" + hashlib.sha256(raw_input.encode()).hexdigest()\\n\\n        injection_result = scan_input(raw_input)\\n        if not injection_result.is_clean:\\n            emit_event(trace_id, \\\"intent_interpreter\\\", \\\"INJECTION_BLOCKED\\\",\\n                       {\\\"risk_score\\\": injection_result.risk_score,\\n                        \\\"matched_patterns\\\": injection_result.matched_patterns})\\n            raise PolicyViolation(f\\\"Input failed injection scan (risk={injection_result.risk_score:.2f})\\\")\\n\\n        emit_event(trace_id, \\\"intent_interpreter\\\", \\\"CLASSIFY_START\\\")\\n\\n        rule_result = _rule_classify(raw_input)\\n        if rule_result:\\n            intent_class, action_type, confidence, ambiguity_score = rule_result\\n            classification_method = \\\"rule\\\"\\n\\n            if ambiguity_score > 0.7:\\n                emit_event(trace_id, \\\"intent_interpreter\\\", \\\"CLARIFICATION_REQUIRED\\\",\\n                           {\\\"ambiguity_score\\\": ambiguity_score})\\n                raise ClarificationRequired(session_id, ambiguity_score)\\n\\n            entity_id, entity_class = _extract_entity(raw_input)\\n            intent = Intent(\\n                session_id=session_id,\\n                intent_class=intent_class,\\n                action_type=ActionType(action_type),\\n                target_entity_id=entity_i...[truncated]"},"type":"raw"},"obs_mqv7ggc8_02a6fd389423":{"observation":{"concepts":["structured output generation","constrained planning","context-aware prompting","plan option generation"],"confidence":1,"facts":["The module handles Step 5 of the pipeline: constrained option generation via LiteLLM.","Uses a structured system prompt to generate N PlanOption objects with specific action types (e.g., READ_FILE, RUN_COMMAND, DEPLOY).</PlanOption>","Integrates with agentmemory to persist generated options for auditing.","Builds context summaries from ContextManifest including recent outcomes (S/P/F counts) and dominant patterns."],"files":["/Users/xnch/xnchSystems/nexi/nexi/pipeline/option_generator.py"],"id":"obs_mqv7ggc8_02a6fd389423","importance":3,"narrative":"Read the implementation of the option generation pipeline. This code defines how the agent proposes alternative actionable plans based on intent and context history.","sessionId":"283b9ba1-0eba-4a0c-ba9d-0cf00eb4bc4b","subtitle":"Inspecting the constrained option generation logic","timestamp":"2026-06-26T17:28:47.242Z","title":"Read option_generator.py","type":"file_read"},"type":"compressed"},"obs_mqv7ggnc_37fc611a7541":{"observation":{"concepts":["DAG compilation","Plan execution pipeline","Action specification validation"],"confidence":1,"facts":["The `compile_action_spec` function converts a `PlanOption` into a single-node `CompiledDAG`.","Supported action types include READ_FILE, WRITE_FILE, RUN_COMMAND, etc.","The compiler performs basic validation on action_spec.type, target, and params."],"files":["/Users/xnch/xnchSystems/nexi/nexi/pipeline/plan_compiler.py"],"id":"obs_mqv7ggnc_37fc611a7541","importance":3,"narrative":"Read the implementation of the plan compiler to understand how plan options are transformed into executable DAGs. This is a key component of the execution pipeline.","sessionId":"283b9ba1-0eba-4a0c-ba9d-0cf00eb4bc4b","subtitle":"Inspecting the plan compilation logic","timestamp":"2026-06-26T17:28:47.641Z","title":"Read plan_compiler.py","type":"file_read"},"type":"compressed"},"obs_mqv7ggtw_df863c73f73c":{"observation":{"hookType":"post_tool_use","id":"obs_mqv7ggtw_df863c73f73c","raw":{"tool_input":{"file_path":"/Users/xnch/xnchSystems/nexi/nexi/character/prompt_loader.py"},"tool_name":"Read","tool_output":{"file":{"content":"from __future__ import annotations\n\nfrom datetime import datetime, timezone\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nimport yaml\n\n\n_CHARACTER_PATH = Path(__file__).parent / \"nexi_character.yaml\"\n\n\ndef load_character() -> dict:\n    with open(_CHARACTER_PATH) as f:\n        return yaml.safe_load(f)\n\n\ndef build_system_prompt(\n    session_memory: list[dict] | None = None,\n    recent_entities: list[str] | None = None,\n) -> str:\n    char = load_character()\n    identity = char[\"identity\"]\n    style = char[\"communication_style\"]\n    now = datetime.now(timezone.utc).strftime(\"%Y-%m-%d %H:%M UTC\")\n\n    parts = [f\"You are {identity['name']}.\", identity[\"persona\"]]\n    parts.append(\"\")\n    parts.append(f\"You address the user as {identity['address_user_as']}.\")\n    parts.append(f\"Communication: {style['verbosity']}, {style['tone']}.\")\n    parts.append(f\"Current time: {now}\")\n    parts.append(\"\")\n\n    if session_memory:\n        parts.append(\"## Session Context\")\n        for mem in session_memory[-5:]:\n            summary = mem.get(\"summary\", mem.get(\"raw_text\", \"\"))\n            parts.append(f\"- {summary}\")\n        parts.append(\"\")\n\n    if recent_entities:\n        parts.append(\"## Known Entities\")\n        for ent in recent_entities:\n            parts.append(f\"- {ent}\")\n        parts.append(\"\")\n\n    return \"\\n\".join(parts)\n\n\ndef get_nexi_system_prompt() -> str:\n    return build_system_prompt()\n","filePath":"/Users/xnch/xnchSystems/nexi/nexi/character/prompt_loader.py","numLines":51,"startLine":1,"totalLines":51},"type":"text"}},"sessionId":"283b9ba1-0eba-4a0c-ba9d-0cf00eb4bc4b","timestamp":"2026-06-26T17:28:47.876Z","toolInput":{"file_path":"/Users/xnch/xnchSystems/nexi/nexi/character/prompt_loader.py"},"toolName":"Read","toolOutput":{"file":{"content":"from __future__ import annotations\n\nfrom datetime import datetime, timezone\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nimport yaml\n\n\n_CHARACTER_PATH = Path(__file__).parent / \"nexi_character.yaml\"\n\n\ndef load_character() -> dict:\n    with open(_CHARACTER_PATH) as f:\n        return yaml.safe_load(f)\n\n\ndef build_system_prompt(\n    session_memory: list[dict] | None = None,\n    recent_entities: list[str] | None = None,\n) -> str:\n    char = load_character()\n    identity = char[\"identity\"]\n    style = char[\"communication_style\"]\n    now = datetime.now(timezone.utc).strftime(\"%Y-%m-%d %H:%M UTC\")\n\n    parts = [f\"You are {identity['name']}.\", identity[\"persona\"]]\n    parts.append(\"\")\n    parts.append(f\"You address the user as {identity['address_user_as']}.\")\n    parts.append(f\"Communication: {style['verbosity']}, {style['tone']}.\")\n    parts.append(f\"Current time: {now}\")\n    parts.append(\"\")\n\n    if session_memory:\n        parts.append(\"## Session Context\")\n        for mem in session_memory[-5:]:\n            summary = mem.get(\"summary\", mem.get(\"raw_text\", \"\"))\n            parts.append(f\"- {summary}\")\n        parts.append(\"\")\n\n    if recent_entities:\n        parts.append(\"## Known Entities\")\n        for ent in recent_entities:\n            parts.append(f\"- {ent}\")\n        parts.append(\"\")\n\n    return \"\\n\".join(parts)\n\n\ndef get_nexi_system_prompt() -> str:\n    return build_system_prompt()\n","filePath":"/Users/xnch/xnchSystems/nexi/nexi/character/prompt_loader.py","numLines":51,"startLine":1,"totalLines":51},"type":"text"}},"type":"raw"},"obs_mqv7gh5s_9fcbecc4b54c":{"observation":{"hookType":"post_tool_use","id":"obs_mqv7gh5s_9fcbecc4b54c","raw":{"tool_input":{"file_path":"/Users/xnch/xnchSystems/nexi/nexi/character/cold_start_seeder.py"},"tool_name":"Read","tool_output":{"file":{"content":"from __future__ import annotations\n\nIDENTITY_FACTS = [\n    {\n        \"type\": \"identity\",\n        \"raw_text\": \"ck-san is a Senior Platform Engineer at Rakuten India in Bengaluru\",\n        \"importance\": 2.0,\n    },\n    {\n        \"type\": \"identity\",\n        \"raw_text\": \"ck-san is pivoting to AI Infrastructure and FDE roles\",\n        \"importance\": 2.0,\n    },\n    {\n        \"type\": \"identity\",\n        \"raw_text\": \"XNCH is the private AI orchestration platform; Nexi is the product interface layer\",\n        \"importance\": 2.0,\n    },\n    {\n        \"type\": \"identity\",\n        \"raw_text\": \"Primary local model: Gemma 4 26B on RTX 3090 at ~135 tok/s\",\n        \"importance\": 2.0,\n    },\n    {\n        \"type\": \"identity\",\n        \"raw_text\": \"ck-san prefers Firefox; never suggest Chrome-based tooling\",\n        \"importance\": 2.0,\n    },\n    {\n        \"type\": \"identity\",\n        \"raw_text\": \"ck-san works solo on XNCH and Nexi — no team, sole ownership\",\n        \"importance\": 2.0,\n    },\n    {\n        \"type\": \"identity\",\n        \"raw_text\": \"Chitradurga relocation is a long-term consideration for remote work lifestyle\",\n        \"importance\": 2.0,\n    },\n]\n\n\nasync def seed_identity_memories(episodic_store) -> int:\n    from xnch.memory.pg_episodic_store import PgEpisodicStore\n\n    if not isinstance(episodic_store, PgEpisodicStore):\n        return 0\n\n    existing = await episodic_store.list_recent(hours=999999)\n    identity_count = sum(1 for m in existing if m.get(\"type\") == \"identity\")\n    if identity_count > 0:\n        return 0\n\n    count = 0\n    for fact in IDENTITY_FACTS:\n        await episodic_store.store_episode(\n            type_=fact[\"type\"],\n            raw_text=fact[\"raw_text\"],\n            importance=fact[\"importance\"],\n        )\n        count += 1\n    return count\n","filePath":"/Users/xnch/xnchSystems/nexi/nexi/character/cold_start_seeder.py","numLines":62,"startLine":1,"totalLines":62},"type":"text"}},"sessionId":"283b9ba1-0eba-4a0c-ba9d-0cf00eb4bc4b","timestamp":"2026-06-26T17:28:48.307Z","toolInput":{"file_path":"/Users/xnch/xnchSystems/nexi/nexi/character/cold_start_seeder.py"},"toolName":"Read","toolOutput":{"file":{"content":"from __future__ import annotations\n\nIDENTITY_FACTS = [\n    {\n        \"type\": \"identity\",\n        \"raw_text\": \"ck-san is a Senior Platform Engineer at Rakuten India in Bengaluru\",\n        \"importance\": 2.0,\n    },\n    {\n        \"type\": \"identity\",\n        \"raw_text\": \"ck-san is pivoting to AI Infrastructure and FDE roles\",\n        \"importance\": 2.0,\n    },\n    {\n        \"type\": \"identity\",\n        \"raw_text\": \"XNCH is the private AI orchestration platform; Nexi is the product interface layer\",\n        \"importance\": 2.0,\n    },\n    {\n        \"type\": \"identity\",\n        \"raw_text\": \"Primary local model: Gemma 4 26B on RTX 3090 at ~135 tok/s\",\n        \"importance\": 2.0,\n    },\n    {\n        \"type\": \"identity\",\n        \"raw_text\": \"ck-san prefers Firefox; never suggest Chrome-based tooling\",\n        \"importance\": 2.0,\n    },\n    {\n        \"type\": \"identity\",\n        \"raw_text\": \"ck-san works solo on XNCH and Nexi — no team, sole ownership\",\n        \"importance\": 2.0,\n    },\n    {\n        \"type\": \"identity\",\n        \"raw_text\": \"Chitradurga relocation is a long-term consideration for remote work lifestyle\",\n        \"importance\": 2.0,\n    },\n]\n\n\nasync def seed_identity_memories(episodic_store) -> int:\n    from xnch.memory.pg_episodic_store import PgEpisodicStore\n\n    if not isinstance(episodic_store, PgEpisodicStore):\n        return 0\n\n    existing = await episodic_store.list_recent(hours=999999)\n    identity_count = sum(1 for m in existing if m.get(\"type\") == \"identity\")\n    if identity_count > 0:\n        return 0\n\n    count = 0\n    for fact in IDENTITY_FACTS:\n        await episodic_store.store_episode(\n            type_=fact[\"type\"],\n            raw_text=fact[\"raw_text\"],\n            importance=fact[\"importance\"],\n        )\n        count += 1\n    return count\n","filePath":"/Users/xnch/xnchSystems/nexi/nexi/character/cold_start_seeder.py","numLines":62,"startLine":1,"totalLines":62},"type":"text"}},"type":"raw"},"obs_mqv7gm12_2e98d14759ac":{"observation":{"hookType":"post_tool_use","id":"obs_mqv7gm12_2e98d14759ac","raw":{"tool_input":{"file_path":"/Users/xnch/xnchSystems/nexi/nexi/proactivity/engine.py"},"tool_name":"Read","tool_output":{"file":{"content":"from __future__ import annotations\n\nimport json\nimport logging\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass, field\nfrom datetime import datetime, timedelta, timezone\nfrom uuid import uuid4\n\nlogger = logging.getLogger(__name__)\n\n\n@dataclass\nclass ProactivityEvent:\n    trigger: str\n    message: str\n    priority: int = 0\n    expires_at: datetime = field(default_factory=lambda: datetime.now(timezone.utc) + timedelta(hours=2))\n\n    @property\n    def expired(self) -> bool:\n        return datetime.now(timezone.utc) > self.expires_at\n\n    def to_dict(self) -> dict:\n        return {\n            \"trigger\": self.trigger,\n            \"message\": self.message,\n            \"priority\": self.priority,\n            \"expires_at\": self.expires_at.isoformat(),\n        }\n\n    @classmethod\n    def from_dict(cls, d: dict) -> ProactivityEvent:\n        return cls(\n            trigger=d[\"trigger\"],\n            message=d[\"message\"],\n            priority=d.get(\"priority\", 0),\n            expires_at=datetime.fromisoformat(d[\"expires_at\"]),\n        )\n\n\nclass ProactivityEngine:\n    def __init__(self, redis_client, http_client=None):\n        self._redis = redis_client\n        self._http = http_client\n\n    async def check_and_queue(\n        self,\n        pattern_store=None,\n        db_path=None,\n    ) -> list[ProactivityEvent]:\n        events: list[ProactivityEvent] = []\n        now = datetime.now(timezone.utc)\n\n        if pattern_store is not None:\n            try:\n                patterns = pattern_store.get_failing_patterns(success_rate_threshold=0.4, min_observations=5)\n                for p in patterns:\n                    events.append(ProactivityEvent(\n                        trigger=\"stale_pattern\",\n                        message=(\n                            f\"ck-san, the {p.get('action_type', 'unknown')} pattern for \"\n                            f\"{p.get('intent_class', 'unknown')} is failing 60%+ of the time. \"\n                            f\"Want me to draft a policy candidate fix?\"\n                        ),\n                        priority=3,\n                        expires_at=now + timedelta(hours=2),\n                    ))\n            except Exception as e:\n                logger.warning(\"Proactivity Rule 1 (stale pattern) failed: %s\", e)\n\n        if db_path is not None:\n            try:\n                import aiosqlite\n                async with aiosqlite.connect(db_path) as db:\n                    async with db.execute(\n                        \"SELECT MAX(run_started_at) FROM consolidation_jobs WHERE status = 'completed'\"\n                    ) as cursor:\n                        row = await cursor.fetchone()\n                if row and row[0]:\n                    last_run = datetime.fromisoformat(row[0])\n                    if (now - last_run) > timedelta(hours=25):\n                        events.append(ProactivityEvent(\n                            trigger=\"consolidation_stale\",\n                            message=\"Consolidation has not run in 25h. Redis working memory may be stale.\",\n                            priority=2,\n                            expires_at=now + timedelta(hours=4),\n                        ))\n            except Exception as e:\n                logger.warning(\"Proactivity Rule 2 (consolidation) failed: %s\", e)\n\n        if self._http is not None:\n            try:\n                resp = await self._http.get(\"http://i9-node:8080/health\")\n                if resp.status_code != 200:\n                    events.append(ProactivityEvent(\n                        trigger=\"inference_down\",\n                        message=\"Gemma 4 on i9 is not responding. Routing fallback to claude-judgment is active.\",\n                        priority=5,\n                        expires_at=now + timedelta(hours=1),\n                    ))\n            except Exception:\n                events.append(ProactivityEvent(\n                    trigger=\"inference_down\",\n                    message=\"Gemma 4 on i9 is not responding. Routing fallback to claude-judgment is active.\",\n                    priority=5,\n                    expires_at=now + timedelta(hours=1),\n                ))\n\n        if db_path is not None:\n            try:\n                import aiosqlite\n                async with aiosqlite.connect(db_path) as db:\n                    async with db.execute(\n                        \"SELECT MAX(run_started_at) FROM extractor_runs WHERE status = 'completed'\"\n                    ) as cursor:\n                        row = await cursor.fetchone()\n                if row and row[0]:\n                    last_extract = datetime.fromisoformat(row[0])\n                    if (now - last_extract) > timedelta(hours=7):\n                        events.append(ProactivityEvent(\n                            trigger=\"learning_loop_silence\",\n                            message=\"Pattern extractor has been silent for 7h. Check xnch-core logs.\",\n                            priority=4,\n                            expires_at=now + timedelta(hours=2),\n                        ))\n            except Exception as e:\n                logger.warning(\"Proactivity Rule 4 (learning silence) failed: %s\", e)\n\n        for ev in events:\n            await self.queue_event(ev)\n\n        return events\n\n    async def queue_event(self, event: ProactivityEvent) -> None:\n        key = f\"proactivity:pending:{uuid4()}\"\n        ttl_seconds = max(60, int((event.expires_at - datetime.now(timezone.utc)).total_seconds()))\n        await self._redis.set(key, json.dumps(event.to_dict()), ex=ttl_seconds)\n\n    async def get_pending(self) -> list[ProactivityEvent]:\n        events: list[ProactivityEvent] = []\n        cursor = 0\n        while True:\n            cursor, keys = await self._redis.scan(cursor=cursor, match=\"proactivity:pending:*\")\n            for k in keys:\n                raw = await self._redis.get(k)\n                if raw is None:\n                    continue\n                try:\n                    ev = ProactivityEvent.from_dict(json.loads(raw))\n                    if not ev.expired:\n                        events.append(ev)\n                except Exception:\n                    pass\n            if cursor == 0:\n                break\n        events.sort(key=lambda e: e.priority, reverse=True)\n        return events\n","filePath":"/Users/xnch/xnchSystems/nexi/nexi/proactivity/engine.py","numLines":158,"startLine":1,"totalLines":158},"type":"text"}},"sessionId":"283b9ba1-0eba-4a0c-ba9d-0cf00eb4bc4b","timestamp":"2026-06-26T17:28:54.616Z","toolInput":{"file_path":"/Users/xnch/xnchSystems/nexi/nexi/proactivity/engine.py"},"toolName":"Read","toolOutput":{"file":{"content":"from __future__ import annotations\n\nimport json\nimport logging\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass, field\nfrom datetime import datetime, timedelta, timezone\nfrom uuid import uuid4\n\nlogger = logging.getLogger(__name__)\n\n\n@dataclass\nclass ProactivityEvent:\n    trigger: str\n    message: str\n    priority: int = 0\n    expires_at: datetime = field(default_factory=lambda: datetime.now(timezone.utc) + timedelta(hours=2))\n\n    @property\n    def expired(self) -> bool:\n        return datetime.now(timezone.utc) > self.expires_at\n\n    def to_dict(self) -> dict:\n        return {\n            \"trigger\": self.trigger,\n            \"message\": self.message,\n            \"priority\": self.priority,\n            \"expires_at\": self.expires_at.isoformat(),\n        }\n\n    @classmethod\n    def from_dict(cls, d: dict) -> ProactivityEvent:\n        return cls(\n            trigger=d[\"trigger\"],\n            message=d[\"message\"],\n            priority=d.get(\"priority\", 0),\n            expires_at=datetime.fromisoformat(d[\"expires_at\"]),\n        )\n\n\nclass ProactivityEngine:\n    def __init__(self, redis_client, http_client=None):\n        self._redis = redis_client\n        self._http = http_client\n\n    async def check_and_queue(\n        self,\n        pattern_store=None,\n        db_path=None,\n    ) -> list[ProactivityEvent]:\n        events: list[ProactivityEvent] = []\n        now = datetime.now(timezone.utc)\n\n        if pattern_store is not None:\n            try:\n                patterns = pattern_store.get_failing_patterns(success_rate_threshold=0.4, min_observations=5)\n                for p in patterns:\n                    events.append(ProactivityEvent(\n                        trigger=\"stale_pattern\",\n                        message=(\n                            f\"ck-san, the {p.get('action_type', 'unknown')} pattern for \"\n                            f\"{p.get('intent_class', 'unknown')} is failing 60%+ of the time. \"\n                            f\"Want me to draft a policy candidate fix?\"\n                        ),\n                        priority=3,\n                        expires_at=now + timedelta(hours=2),\n                    ))\n            except Exception as e:\n                logger.warning(\"Proactivity Rule 1 (stale pattern) failed: %s\", e)\n\n        if db_path is not None:\n            try:\n                import aiosqlite\n                async with aiosqlite.connect(db_path) as db:\n                    async with db.execute(\n                        \"SELECT MAX(run_started_at) FROM consolidation_jobs WHERE status = 'completed'\"\n                    ) as cursor:\n                        row = await cursor.fetchone()\n                if row and row[0]:\n                    last_run = datetime.fromisoformat(row[0])\n                    if (now - last_run) > timedelta(hours=25):\n                        events.append(ProactivityEvent(\n                            trigger=\"consolidation_stale\",\n                            message=\"Consolidation has not run in 25h. Redis working memory may be stale.\",\n                            priority=2,\n                            expires_at=now + timedelta(hours=4),\n                        ))\n            except Exception as e:\n                logger.warning(\"Proactivity Rule 2 (consolidation) failed: %s\", e)\n\n        if self._http is not None:\n            try:\n                resp = await self._http.get(\"http://i9-node:8080/health\")\n                if resp.status_code != 200:\n                    events.append(ProactivityEvent(\n                        trigger=\"inference_down\",\n                        message=\"Gemma 4 on i9 is not responding. Routing fallback to claude-judgment is active.\",\n                        priority=5,\n                        expires_at=now + timedelta(hours=1),\n                    ))\n            except Exception:\n                events.append(ProactivityEvent(\n                    trigger=\"inference_down\",\n                    message=\"Gemma 4 on i9 is not responding. Routing fallback to claude-judgment is active.\",\n                    priority=5,\n                    expires_at=now + timedelta(hours=1),\n                ))\n\n        if db_path is not None:\n            try:\n                import aiosqlite\n                async with aiosqlite.connect(db_path) as db:\n                    async with db.execute(\n                        \"SELECT MAX(run_started_at) FROM extractor_runs WHERE status = 'completed'\"\n                    ) as cursor:\n                        row = await cursor.fetchone()\n                if row and row[0]:\n                    last_extract = datetime.fromisoformat(row[0])\n                    if (now - last_extract) > timedelta(hours=7):\n                        events.append(ProactivityEvent(\n                            trigger=\"learning_loop_silence\",\n                            message=\"Pattern extractor has been silent for 7h. Check xnch-core logs.\",\n                            priority=4,\n                            expires_at=now + timedelta(hours=2),\n                        ))\n            except Exception as e:\n                logger.warning(\"Proactivity Rule 4 (learning silence) failed: %s\", e)\n\n        for ev in events:\n            await self.queue_event(ev)\n\n        return events\n\n    async def queue_event(self, event: ProactivityEvent) -> None:\n        key = f\"proactivity:pending:{uuid4()}\"\n        ttl_seconds = max(60, int((event.expires_at - datetime.now(timezone.utc)).total_seconds()))\n        await self._redis.set(key, json.dumps(event.to_dict()), ex=ttl_seconds)\n\n    async def get_pending(self) -> list[ProactivityEvent]:\n        events: list[ProactivityEvent] = []\n        cursor = 0\n        while True:\n            cursor, keys = await self._redis.scan(cursor=cursor, match=\"proactivity:pending:*\")\n            for k in keys:\n                raw = await self._redis.get(k)\n                if raw is None:\n                    continue\n                try:\n                    ev = ProactivityEvent.from_dict(json.loads(raw))\n                    if not ev.expired:\n                        events.append(ev)\n                except Exception:\n                    pass\n            if cursor == 0:\n                break\n        events.sort(key=lambda e: e.priority, reverse=True)\n        return events\n","filePath":"/Users/xnch/xnchSystems/nexi/nexi/proactivity/engine.py","numLines":158,"startLine":1,"totalLines":158},"type":"text"}},"type":"raw"},"obs_mqv7gm8z_8025abe5569f":{"observation":{"hookType":"post_tool_use","id":"obs_mqv7gm8z_8025abe5569f","raw":{"tool_input":{"file_path":"/Users/xnch/xnchSystems/xnch/xnch/routes/nexi_gateway.py"},"tool_name":"Read","tool_output":"{\"type\":\"text\",\"file\":{\"filePath\":\"/Users/xnch/xnchSystems/xnch/xnch/routes/nexi_gateway.py\",\"content\":\"import json\\nimport logging\\nimport os\\nfrom typing import Any\\nfrom uuid import uuid4\\n\\nimport httpx\\nfrom fastapi import APIRouter, HTTPException, Request\\nfrom fastapi.responses import PlainTextResponse, StreamingResponse\\nfrom pydantic import BaseModel\\n\\nfrom nexi.character.prompt_loader import build_system_prompt\\nfrom nexi.pipeline.context_assembler import assemble_context\\nfrom nexi.proactivity.engine import ProactivityEngine\\nfrom xnch.routing.classifier import classify_request\\nfrom xnch.security.injection_guard import scan_input\\n\\nlogger = logging.getLogger(__name__)\\nrouter = APIRouter(prefix=\\\"/nexi\\\", tags=[\\\"nexi\\\"])\\n\\nSYSTEM_PROMPT_CACHE_KEY = \\\"nexi:system-prompt\\\"\\nSYSTEM_PROMPT_CACHE_TTL = 60\\n\\nLITELLM_BASE = os.environ.get(\\\"LITELLM_BASE_URL\\\", \\\"http://i7-node:4000\\\")\\nLITELLM_API_KEY = os.environ.get(\\\"LITELLM_API_KEY\\\", \\\"\\\")\\n\\n\\nclass ChatRequest(BaseModel):\\n    session_id: str\\n    message: str\\n    actor_role: str = \\\"openclaw\\\"\\n\\n\\nclass MemoryRecallRequest(BaseModel):\\n    query: str\\n    top_k: int = 5\\n\\n\\ndef _get_proactivity(app) -> ProactivityEngine:\\n    if not hasattr(app, \\\"_nexi_proactivity\\\"):\\n        redis = app.kv_cache._redis\\n        app._nexi_proactivity = ProactivityEngine(redis)\\n    return app._nexi_proactivity\\n\\n\\ndef _invalidate_system_prompt_cache(app) -> None:\\n    redis = app.kv_cache._redis\\n    try:\\n        import asyncio\\n        asyncio.ensure_future(redis.delete(SYSTEM_PROMPT_CACHE_KEY))\\n    except Exception:\\n        pass\\n\\n\\n@router.get(\\\"/system-prompt\\\", response_class=PlainTextResponse)\\nasync def get_system_prompt(request: Request) -> str:\\n    app = request.app.state\\n    redis = app.kv_cache._redis\\n\\n    cached = await redis.get(SYSTEM_PROMPT_CACHE_KEY)\\n    if cached:\\n        return cached\\n\\n    from agentmemory import get_memories\\n    entities = get_memories(\\\"entities\\\", n_results=20)\\n    recent_entities = [e.get(\\\"document\\\", \\\"\\\") for e in entities if e.get(\\\"document\\\")]\\n\\n    prompt = build_system_prompt(session_memory=[], recent_entities=recent_entities)\\n    await redis.set(SYSTEM_PROMPT_CACHE_KEY, prompt, ex=SYSTEM_PROMPT_CACHE_TTL)\\n    return prompt\\n\\n\\n@router.post(\\\"/chat\\\")\\nasync def chat(body: ChatRequest, request: Request) -> dict[str, Any]:\\n    app = request.app.state\\n\\n    result = scan_input(body.message, app.event_log)\\n    if not result.is_clean:\\n        raise HTTPException(status_code=400, detail=\\\"Input rejected by injection guard\\\")\\n\\n    ctx = await assemble_context(\\n        session_id=body.session_id,\\n        raw_input=body.message,\\n        working_memory=app.working_memory,\\n        pg_episodic=app.pg_episodic,\\n        graph_store=app.graph_store,\\n        relationship_store=app.relationship_store,\\n        sensory_buffer=app.sensory_buffer,\\n        proactivity_engine=_get_proactivity(app),\\n    )\\n\\n    route = classify_request(body.message, body.actor_role, {})\\n    messages = ctx.to_messages(body.message)\\n    model_name = route.model_name\\n\\n    try:\\n        async with httpx.AsyncClient(base_url=LITELLM_BASE, timeout=120.0) as client:\\n            resp = await client.post(\\n                \\\"/chat/completions\\\",\\n                json={\\n                    \\\"model\\\": model_name,\\n                    \\\"messages\\\": messages,\\n                    \\\"max_tokens\\\": 2048,\\n                    \\\"temperature\\\": 0.7,\\n                },\\n                headers={\\\"Authorization\\\": f\\\"Bearer {LITELLM_API_KEY}\\\"} if LITELLM_API_KEY else {},\\n            )\\n            resp.raise_for_status()\\n            response_text = resp.json()[\\\"choices\\\"][0][\\\"message\\\"][\\\"content\\\"]\\n    except Exception as exc:\\n        logger.error(\\\"LiteLLM call failed: %s\\\", exc)\\n        raise HTTPException(status_code=502, detail=\\\"LiteLLM unavailable\\\")\\n\\n    await app.working_memory.append_turn(body.session_id, \\\"user\\\", body.message)\\n    await app.working_memory.append_turn(body.session_id, \\\"assistant\\\", response_text)\\n\\n    await app.pg_episodic.store_episode(\\n        type_=\\\"conversation\\\",\\n        raw_text=f\\\"{body.message}\\\\n{response_text}\\\",\\n        summary=f\\\"OpenClaw chat: {body.message[:100]}\\\",\\n    )\\n\\n    _invalidate_system_prompt_cache(app)\\n\\n    return {\\n        \\\"response\\\": response_text,\\n        \\\"model_used\\\": model_name,\\n        \\\"session_id\\\": body.session_id,\\n    }\\n\\n\\n@router.post(\\\"/chat/stream\\\")\\nasync def chat_stream(body: ChatRequest, request: Request) -> StreamingResponse:\\n    app = request.app.state\\n\\n    result = scan_input(body.message, app.event_log)\\n    if not result.is_clean:\\n        raise HTTPException(status_code=400, detail=\\\"Input rejected by injection guard\\\")\\n\\n    ctx = await assemble_context(\\n        session_id=body.session_id,\\n        raw_input=body.message,\\n        working_memory=app.working_memory,\\n        pg_episodic=app.pg_episodic,\\n        graph_store=app.graph_store,\\n        relationship_store=app.relationship_store,\\n        sensory_buffer=app.sensory_buffer,\\n        proactivity_engine=_get_proactivity(app),\\n    )\\n\\n    route = classify_request(body.message, body.actor_role, {})\\n    messages = ctx.to_messages(body.message)\\n    model_name = route.model_name\\n\\n    await app.working_memory.append_turn(body.session_id, \\\"user\\\", body.message)\\n\\n    async def event_stream():\\n        full_text = \\\"\\\"\\n        try:\\n            async with httpx.AsyncClient(base_url=LITELLM_BASE, timeout=120.0) as client:\\n                async with client.stream(\\n                    \\\"POST\\\",\\n                    \\\"/chat/completions\\\",\\n                    json={\\n                        \\\"model\\\": model_name,\\n                        \\\"messages\\\": messages,\\n                        \\\"max_tokens\\\": 2048,\\n                        \\\"temperature\\\": 0.7,\\n                        \\\"stream\\\": True,\\n                    },\\n                    headers={\\\"Authorization\\\": f\\\"Bearer {LITELLM_API_KEY}\\\"} if LITELLM_API_KEY else {},\\n                ) as resp:\\n                    if resp.status_code != 200:\\n                        yield f\\\"data: {json.dumps({'error': f'LiteLLM error {resp.status_code}'})}\\\\n\\\\n\\\"\\n                        yield \\\"data: [DONE]\\\\n\\\\n\\\"\\n                        return\\n                    async for line in resp.aiter_lines():\\n                        if not line.startswith(\\\"data: \\\"):\\n                            continue\\n                        payload = line.removeprefix(\\\"data: \\\")\\n                        if payload == \\\"[DONE]\\\":\\n                            break\\n                        try:\\n                            chunk = json.loads(payload)\\n                            delta = chunk.get(\\\"choices\\\", [{}])[0].get(\\\"delta\\\", {}).get(\\\"content\\\", \\\"\\\")\\n                            if delta:\\n                                full_text += delta\\n                                yield f\\\"data: {json.dumps({'content': delta})}\\\\n\\\\n\\\"\\n                        except json.JSONDecodeError:\\n                            continue\\n        except Exception as exc:\\n            logger.error(\\\"LiteLLM stream failed: %s\\\", exc)\\n            yield f\\\"data: {json.dumps({'error': 'LiteLLM unavailable'})}\\\\n\\\\n\\\"\\n            yield \\\"data: [DONE]\\\\n\\\\n\\\"\\n            return\\n\\n        await app.working_memory.append_turn(body.session_id, \\\"assistant\\\", full_text)\\n        await app.pg_episodic.store_episode(\\n            type_=\\\"conversation\\\",\\n            raw_text=f\\\"{body.message}\\\\n{full_text}\\\",\\n            summary=f\\\"OpenClaw chat: {body.message[:100]}\\\",\\n        )\\n        _invalidate_system_prompt_cache(app)\\n        yield \\\"data: [DONE]\\\\n\\\\n\\\"\\n\\n    return StreamingResponse(event_stream(), media_type=\\\"text/event-stream\\\")\\n\\n\\n@router.get(\\\"/memory/surface\\\")\\nasync def memory_surface(request: Request) -> list[dict[str, Any]]:\\n    app = request.app.state\\n    proa...[truncated]"},"sessionId":"283b9ba1-0eba-4a0c-ba9d-0cf00eb4bc4b","timestamp":"2026-06-26T17:28:54.899Z","toolInput":{"file_path":"/Users/xnch/xnchSystems/xnch/xnch/routes/nexi_gateway.py"},"toolName":"Read","toolOutput":"{\"type\":\"text\",\"file\":{\"filePath\":\"/Users/xnch/xnchSystems/xnch/xnch/routes/nexi_gateway.py\",\"content\":\"import json\\nimport logging\\nimport os\\nfrom typing import Any\\nfrom uuid import uuid4\\n\\nimport httpx\\nfrom fastapi import APIRouter, HTTPException, Request\\nfrom fastapi.responses import PlainTextResponse, StreamingResponse\\nfrom pydantic import BaseModel\\n\\nfrom nexi.character.prompt_loader import build_system_prompt\\nfrom nexi.pipeline.context_assembler import assemble_context\\nfrom nexi.proactivity.engine import ProactivityEngine\\nfrom xnch.routing.classifier import classify_request\\nfrom xnch.security.injection_guard import scan_input\\n\\nlogger = logging.getLogger(__name__)\\nrouter = APIRouter(prefix=\\\"/nexi\\\", tags=[\\\"nexi\\\"])\\n\\nSYSTEM_PROMPT_CACHE_KEY = \\\"nexi:system-prompt\\\"\\nSYSTEM_PROMPT_CACHE_TTL = 60\\n\\nLITELLM_BASE = os.environ.get(\\\"LITELLM_BASE_URL\\\", \\\"http://i7-node:4000\\\")\\nLITELLM_API_KEY = os.environ.get(\\\"LITELLM_API_KEY\\\", \\\"\\\")\\n\\n\\nclass ChatRequest(BaseModel):\\n    session_id: str\\n    message: str\\n    actor_role: str = \\\"openclaw\\\"\\n\\n\\nclass MemoryRecallRequest(BaseModel):\\n    query: str\\n    top_k: int = 5\\n\\n\\ndef _get_proactivity(app) -> ProactivityEngine:\\n    if not hasattr(app, \\\"_nexi_proactivity\\\"):\\n        redis = app.kv_cache._redis\\n        app._nexi_proactivity = ProactivityEngine(redis)\\n    return app._nexi_proactivity\\n\\n\\ndef _invalidate_system_prompt_cache(app) -> None:\\n    redis = app.kv_cache._redis\\n    try:\\n        import asyncio\\n        asyncio.ensure_future(redis.delete(SYSTEM_PROMPT_CACHE_KEY))\\n    except Exception:\\n        pass\\n\\n\\n@router.get(\\\"/system-prompt\\\", response_class=PlainTextResponse)\\nasync def get_system_prompt(request: Request) -> str:\\n    app = request.app.state\\n    redis = app.kv_cache._redis\\n\\n    cached = await redis.get(SYSTEM_PROMPT_CACHE_KEY)\\n    if cached:\\n        return cached\\n\\n    from agentmemory import get_memories\\n    entities = get_memories(\\\"entities\\\", n_results=20)\\n    recent_entities = [e.get(\\\"document\\\", \\\"\\\") for e in entities if e.get(\\\"document\\\")]\\n\\n    prompt = build_system_prompt(session_memory=[], recent_entities=recent_entities)\\n    await redis.set(SYSTEM_PROMPT_CACHE_KEY, prompt, ex=SYSTEM_PROMPT_CACHE_TTL)\\n    return prompt\\n\\n\\n@router.post(\\\"/chat\\\")\\nasync def chat(body: ChatRequest, request: Request) -> dict[str, Any]:\\n    app = request.app.state\\n\\n    result = scan_input(body.message, app.event_log)\\n    if not result.is_clean:\\n        raise HTTPException(status_code=400, detail=\\\"Input rejected by injection guard\\\")\\n\\n    ctx = await assemble_context(\\n        session_id=body.session_id,\\n        raw_input=body.message,\\n        working_memory=app.working_memory,\\n        pg_episodic=app.pg_episodic,\\n        graph_store=app.graph_store,\\n        relationship_store=app.relationship_store,\\n        sensory_buffer=app.sensory_buffer,\\n        proactivity_engine=_get_proactivity(app),\\n    )\\n\\n    route = classify_request(body.message, body.actor_role, {})\\n    messages = ctx.to_messages(body.message)\\n    model_name = route.model_name\\n\\n    try:\\n        async with httpx.AsyncClient(base_url=LITELLM_BASE, timeout=120.0) as client:\\n            resp = await client.post(\\n                \\\"/chat/completions\\\",\\n                json={\\n                    \\\"model\\\": model_name,\\n                    \\\"messages\\\": messages,\\n                    \\\"max_tokens\\\": 2048,\\n                    \\\"temperature\\\": 0.7,\\n                },\\n                headers={\\\"Authorization\\\": f\\\"Bearer {LITELLM_API_KEY}\\\"} if LITELLM_API_KEY else {},\\n            )\\n            resp.raise_for_status()\\n            response_text = resp.json()[\\\"choices\\\"][0][\\\"message\\\"][\\\"content\\\"]\\n    except Exception as exc:\\n        logger.error(\\\"LiteLLM call failed: %s\\\", exc)\\n        raise HTTPException(status_code=502, detail=\\\"LiteLLM unavailable\\\")\\n\\n    await app.working_memory.append_turn(body.session_id, \\\"user\\\", body.message)\\n    await app.working_memory.append_turn(body.session_id, \\\"assistant\\\", response_text)\\n\\n    await app.pg_episodic.store_episode(\\n        type_=\\\"conversation\\\",\\n        raw_text=f\\\"{body.message}\\\\n{response_text}\\\",\\n        summary=f\\\"OpenClaw chat: {body.message[:100]}\\\",\\n    )\\n\\n    _invalidate_system_prompt_cache(app)\\n\\n    return {\\n        \\\"response\\\": response_text,\\n        \\\"model_used\\\": model_name,\\n        \\\"session_id\\\": body.session_id,\\n    }\\n\\n\\n@router.post(\\\"/chat/stream\\\")\\nasync def chat_stream(body: ChatRequest, request: Request) -> StreamingResponse:\\n    app = request.app.state\\n\\n    result = scan_input(body.message, app.event_log)\\n    if not result.is_clean:\\n        raise HTTPException(status_code=400, detail=\\\"Input rejected by injection guard\\\")\\n\\n    ctx = await assemble_context(\\n        session_id=body.session_id,\\n        raw_input=body.message,\\n        working_memory=app.working_memory,\\n        pg_episodic=app.pg_episodic,\\n        graph_store=app.graph_store,\\n        relationship_store=app.relationship_store,\\n        sensory_buffer=app.sensory_buffer,\\n        proactivity_engine=_get_proactivity(app),\\n    )\\n\\n    route = classify_request(body.message, body.actor_role, {})\\n    messages = ctx.to_messages(body.message)\\n    model_name = route.model_name\\n\\n    await app.working_memory.append_turn(body.session_id, \\\"user\\\", body.message)\\n\\n    async def event_stream():\\n        full_text = \\\"\\\"\\n        try:\\n            async with httpx.AsyncClient(base_url=LITELLM_BASE, timeout=120.0) as client:\\n                async with client.stream(\\n                    \\\"POST\\\",\\n                    \\\"/chat/completions\\\",\\n                    json={\\n                        \\\"model\\\": model_name,\\n                        \\\"messages\\\": messages,\\n                        \\\"max_tokens\\\": 2048,\\n                        \\\"temperature\\\": 0.7,\\n                        \\\"stream\\\": True,\\n                    },\\n                    headers={\\\"Authorization\\\": f\\\"Bearer {LITELLM_API_KEY}\\\"} if LITELLM_API_KEY else {},\\n                ) as resp:\\n                    if resp.status_code != 200:\\n                        yield f\\\"data: {json.dumps({'error': f'LiteLLM error {resp.status_code}'})}\\\\n\\\\n\\\"\\n                        yield \\\"data: [DONE]\\\\n\\\\n\\\"\\n                        return\\n                    async for line in resp.aiter_lines():\\n                        if not line.startswith(\\\"data: \\\"):\\n                            continue\\n                        payload = line.removeprefix(\\\"data: \\\")\\n                        if payload == \\\"[DONE]\\\":\\n                            break\\n                        try:\\n                            chunk = json.loads(payload)\\n                            delta = chunk.get(\\\"choices\\\", [{}])[0].get(\\\"delta\\\", {}).get(\\\"content\\\", \\\"\\\")\\n                            if delta:\\n                                full_text += delta\\n                                yield f\\\"data: {json.dumps({'content': delta})}\\\\n\\\\n\\\"\\n                        except json.JSONDecodeError:\\n                            continue\\n        except Exception as exc:\\n            logger.error(\\\"LiteLLM stream failed: %s\\\", exc)\\n            yield f\\\"data: {json.dumps({'error': 'LiteLLM unavailable'})}\\\\n\\\\n\\\"\\n            yield \\\"data: [DONE]\\\\n\\\\n\\\"\\n            return\\n\\n        await app.working_memory.append_turn(body.session_id, \\\"assistant\\\", full_text)\\n        await app.pg_episodic.store_episode(\\n            type_=\\\"conversation\\\",\\n            raw_text=f\\\"{body.message}\\\\n{full_text}\\\",\\n            summary=f\\\"OpenClaw chat: {body.message[:100]}\\\",\\n        )\\n        _invalidate_system_prompt_cache(app)\\n        yield \\\"data: [DONE]\\\\n\\\\n\\\"\\n\\n    return StreamingResponse(event_stream(), media_type=\\\"text/event-stream\\\")\\n\\n\\n@router.get(\\\"/memory/surface\\\")\\nasync def memory_surface(request: Request) -> list[dict[str, Any]]:\\n    app = request.app.state\\n    proa...[truncated]"},"type":"raw"},"obs_mqv7gmje_ac2e462a4d9f":{"observation":{"hookType":"post_tool_use","id":"obs_mqv7gmje_ac2e462a4d9f","raw":{"tool_input":{"file_path":"/Users/xnch/xnchSystems/xnch/xnch/main.py"},"tool_name":"Read","tool_output":{"file":{"content":"\"\"\"xnch-server v0 — governance, memory, and authorization service.\"\"\"\nimport logging\nfrom contextlib import asynccontextmanager\nfrom starlette.requests import Request\nfrom apscheduler.schedulers.asyncio import AsyncIOScheduler\nfrom fastapi import FastAPI\n\nfrom .auth import load_or_generate_keypair, GovernanceStore, TokenSigner, TokenVerifier\nfrom .audit import EventLog, DecisionLedger\nfrom .config import settings\nfrom .learning import PatternExtractor, ScoreAdapter, PolicyCandidateGenerator\nfrom .memory import init_db, EpisodicStore, PatternStore, KVCache, PgEpisodicStore\nfrom .memory import SensoryBuffer, WorkingMemory, GraphStore, RelationshipStore\nfrom .memory.db import get_state_version, get_policy_version, increment_state_version\nfrom .policy import PolicyLoader, PolicyEngine\nfrom .routes import (\n    session_router, memory_router, policy_router,\n    verdict_router, execution_router, governance_router, auth_router,\n    nexi_gateway_router,\n)\n\nlogger = logging.getLogger(__name__)\n\n\n@asynccontextmanager\nasync def lifespan(app: FastAPI):\n    s = app.state\n\n    # Ensure directories\n    for d in [settings.base_dir, settings.keys_dir, settings.audit_dir,\n              settings.governance_dir, settings.policies_dir, settings.weights_dir]:\n        d.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n\n    # DB init\n    await init_db(settings.db_path)\n\n    # Auth\n    s.keypair = load_or_generate_keypair(settings.keys_dir)\n    s.token_signer = TokenSigner(s.keypair.private_pem)\n    s.token_verifier = TokenVerifier(settings.auth_secret)\n    s.governance = GovernanceStore(settings.db_path)\n    await s.governance.bootstrap()\n\n    # Memory\n    s.episodic = EpisodicStore(settings.db_path)\n    s.pattern_store = PatternStore(settings.db_path)\n    s.kv_cache = KVCache(settings.redis_url)\n\n    # Audit\n    s.event_log = EventLog(settings.audit_dir / \"events.jsonl\")\n    s.ledger = DecisionLedger(settings.audit_dir / \"decisions.jsonl\")\n\n    # Policy\n    _sync_policies(settings)\n    loader = PolicyLoader(settings.policies_dir)\n    policy_set = loader.load()\n    s.policy_engine = PolicyEngine(policy_set)\n    s.policy_loader = loader\n\n    # PG episodic store (production backend)\n    s.pg_episodic = PgEpisodicStore(settings.postgres_url)\n    await s.pg_episodic.connect()\n\n    # Layer 0 — Sensory buffer (Redis perception signals)\n    s.sensory_buffer = SensoryBuffer(settings.redis_url)\n\n    # Layer 1 — Working memory (Redis session context)\n    s.working_memory = WorkingMemory(settings.redis_url)\n\n    # Layer 3 — Graph store (agentmemory semantic graph)\n    s.relationship_store = RelationshipStore(settings.postgres_url)\n    await s.relationship_store.connect()\n    s.graph_store = GraphStore(db_path=settings.db_path, relationship_store=s.relationship_store)\n    s.graph_store.connect()\n\n    # Cold-start seed identity memories on first boot\n    from nexi.character.cold_start_seeder import seed_identity_memories\n    await seed_identity_memories(s.pg_episodic)\n\n    # Learning\n    s.pattern_extractor = PatternExtractor(s.pg_episodic, s.pattern_store)\n    s.score_adapter = ScoreAdapter(settings.db_path)\n    s.policy_candidates = PolicyCandidateGenerator(s.pattern_store, settings.db_path)\n\n    # Convenience helpers for routes\n    async def _get_state_version() -> str:\n        return await get_state_version(settings.db_path)\n\n    async def _get_policy_version() -> str:\n        return await get_policy_version(settings.db_path)\n\n    async def _increment_state_version() -> str:\n        v = await increment_state_version(settings.db_path)\n        logger.info(\"system_state_version incremented to %s\", v)\n        return v\n\n    s.get_state_version = _get_state_version\n    s.get_policy_version = _get_policy_version\n    s.increment_state_version = _increment_state_version\n\n    # Scheduler\n    scheduler = AsyncIOScheduler()\n    scheduler.add_job(\n        lambda: __import__('asyncio').get_event_loop().create_task(\n            s.pattern_extractor.run()\n        ),\n        \"cron\", hour=\"*/6\", id=\"pattern_extractor\",\n    )\n    scheduler.add_job(\n        lambda: __import__('asyncio').get_event_loop().create_task(\n            s.score_adapter.evaluate()\n        ),\n        \"cron\", hour=\"*/6\", minute=30, id=\"score_adapter\",\n    )\n    scheduler.add_job(\n        lambda: __import__('asyncio').get_event_loop().create_task(\n            s.policy_candidates.run()\n        ),\n        \"cron\", hour=\"*/6\", minute=45, id=\"policy_candidates\",\n    )\n    scheduler.start()\n    s.scheduler = scheduler\n\n    s.event_log.emit(\"startup\", \"xnch\", \"SERVER_STARTED\", data={\"version\": \"0.1.0\"})\n    logger.info(\"xnch-server started\")\n\n    yield\n\n    scheduler.shutdown(wait=False)\n    await s.kv_cache.aclose()\n    await s.sensory_buffer.aclose()\n    await s.working_memory.aclose()\n    await s.relationship_store.close()\n    await s.pg_episodic.close()\n    s.event_log.emit(\"shutdown\", \"xnch\", \"SERVER_STOPPED\")\n\n\napp = FastAPI(title=\"xnch\", version=\"0.1.0\", lifespan=lifespan)\n\napp.include_router(session_router)\napp.include_router(memory_router)\napp.include_router(policy_router)\napp.include_router(verdict_router)\napp.include_router(execution_router)\napp.include_router(governance_router)\napp.include_router(auth_router)\napp.include_router(nexi_gateway_router)\n\n\n@app.get(\"/health\")\nasync def health(request: Request) -> dict:\n    redis_ok = await request.app.state.kv_cache.ping()\n    state_version = await request.app.state.get_state_version()\n    return {\n        \"status\": \"ok\" if redis_ok else \"degraded\",\n        \"redis\": \"ok\" if redis_ok else \"unavailable\",\n        \"state_version\": state_version,\n        \"version\": \"0.1.0\",\n    }\n\n\n@app.get(\"/system/state\")\nasync def system_state(request: Request) -> dict:\n    state_version = await request.app.state.get_state_version()\n    policy_version = await request.app.state.get_policy_version()\n    return {\"system_state_version\": state_version, \"policy_version\": policy_version}\n\n\ndef _sync_policies(s) -> None:\n    \"\"\"Copy bundled default policy to ~/.xnch/policies/ if not already present.\"\"\"\n    import pathlib, shutil\n    bundled = pathlib.Path(__file__).parent.parent.parent / \"policies\" / \"default.yaml\"\n    target = s.policies_dir / \"default.yaml\"\n    if bundled.exists() and not target.exists():\n        shutil.copy(bundled, target)\n","filePath":"/Users/xnch/xnchSystems/xnch/xnch/main.py","numLines":176,"startLine":1,"totalLines":176},"type":"text"}},"sessionId":"283b9ba1-0eba-4a0c-ba9d-0cf00eb4bc4b","timestamp":"2026-06-26T17:28:55.277Z","toolInput":{"file_path":"/Users/xnch/xnchSystems/xnch/xnch/main.py"},"toolName":"Read","toolOutput":{"file":{"content":"\"\"\"xnch-server v0 — governance, memory, and authorization service.\"\"\"\nimport logging\nfrom contextlib import asynccontextmanager\nfrom starlette.requests import Request\nfrom apscheduler.schedulers.asyncio import AsyncIOScheduler\nfrom fastapi import FastAPI\n\nfrom .auth import load_or_generate_keypair, GovernanceStore, TokenSigner, TokenVerifier\nfrom .audit import EventLog, DecisionLedger\nfrom .config import settings\nfrom .learning import PatternExtractor, ScoreAdapter, PolicyCandidateGenerator\nfrom .memory import init_db, EpisodicStore, PatternStore, KVCache, PgEpisodicStore\nfrom .memory import SensoryBuffer, WorkingMemory, GraphStore, RelationshipStore\nfrom .memory.db import get_state_version, get_policy_version, increment_state_version\nfrom .policy import PolicyLoader, PolicyEngine\nfrom .routes import (\n    session_router, memory_router, policy_router,\n    verdict_router, execution_router, governance_router, auth_router,\n    nexi_gateway_router,\n)\n\nlogger = logging.getLogger(__name__)\n\n\n@asynccontextmanager\nasync def lifespan(app: FastAPI):\n    s = app.state\n\n    # Ensure directories\n    for d in [settings.base_dir, settings.keys_dir, settings.audit_dir,\n              settings.governance_dir, settings.policies_dir, settings.weights_dir]:\n        d.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n\n    # DB init\n    await init_db(settings.db_path)\n\n    # Auth\n    s.keypair = load_or_generate_keypair(settings.keys_dir)\n    s.token_signer = TokenSigner(s.keypair.private_pem)\n    s.token_verifier = TokenVerifier(settings.auth_secret)\n    s.governance = GovernanceStore(settings.db_path)\n    await s.governance.bootstrap()\n\n    # Memory\n    s.episodic = EpisodicStore(settings.db_path)\n    s.pattern_store = PatternStore(settings.db_path)\n    s.kv_cache = KVCache(settings.redis_url)\n\n    # Audit\n    s.event_log = EventLog(settings.audit_dir / \"events.jsonl\")\n    s.ledger = DecisionLedger(settings.audit_dir / \"decisions.jsonl\")\n\n    # Policy\n    _sync_policies(settings)\n    loader = PolicyLoader(settings.policies_dir)\n    policy_set = loader.load()\n    s.policy_engine = PolicyEngine(policy_set)\n    s.policy_loader = loader\n\n    # PG episodic store (production backend)\n    s.pg_episodic = PgEpisodicStore(settings.postgres_url)\n    await s.pg_episodic.connect()\n\n    # Layer 0 — Sensory buffer (Redis perception signals)\n    s.sensory_buffer = SensoryBuffer(settings.redis_url)\n\n    # Layer 1 — Working memory (Redis session context)\n    s.working_memory = WorkingMemory(settings.redis_url)\n\n    # Layer 3 — Graph store (agentmemory semantic graph)\n    s.relationship_store = RelationshipStore(settings.postgres_url)\n    await s.relationship_store.connect()\n    s.graph_store = GraphStore(db_path=settings.db_path, relationship_store=s.relationship_store)\n    s.graph_store.connect()\n\n    # Cold-start seed identity memories on first boot\n    from nexi.character.cold_start_seeder import seed_identity_memories\n    await seed_identity_memories(s.pg_episodic)\n\n    # Learning\n    s.pattern_extractor = PatternExtractor(s.pg_episodic, s.pattern_store)\n    s.score_adapter = ScoreAdapter(settings.db_path)\n    s.policy_candidates = PolicyCandidateGenerator(s.pattern_store, settings.db_path)\n\n    # Convenience helpers for routes\n    async def _get_state_version() -> str:\n        return await get_state_version(settings.db_path)\n\n    async def _get_policy_version() -> str:\n        return await get_policy_version(settings.db_path)\n\n    async def _increment_state_version() -> str:\n        v = await increment_state_version(settings.db_path)\n        logger.info(\"system_state_version incremented to %s\", v)\n        return v\n\n    s.get_state_version = _get_state_version\n    s.get_policy_version = _get_policy_version\n    s.increment_state_version = _increment_state_version\n\n    # Scheduler\n    scheduler = AsyncIOScheduler()\n    scheduler.add_job(\n        lambda: __import__('asyncio').get_event_loop().create_task(\n            s.pattern_extractor.run()\n        ),\n        \"cron\", hour=\"*/6\", id=\"pattern_extractor\",\n    )\n    scheduler.add_job(\n        lambda: __import__('asyncio').get_event_loop().create_task(\n            s.score_adapter.evaluate()\n        ),\n        \"cron\", hour=\"*/6\", minute=30, id=\"score_adapter\",\n    )\n    scheduler.add_job(\n        lambda: __import__('asyncio').get_event_loop().create_task(\n            s.policy_candidates.run()\n        ),\n        \"cron\", hour=\"*/6\", minute=45, id=\"policy_candidates\",\n    )\n    scheduler.start()\n    s.scheduler = scheduler\n\n    s.event_log.emit(\"startup\", \"xnch\", \"SERVER_STARTED\", data={\"version\": \"0.1.0\"})\n    logger.info(\"xnch-server started\")\n\n    yield\n\n    scheduler.shutdown(wait=False)\n    await s.kv_cache.aclose()\n    await s.sensory_buffer.aclose()\n    await s.working_memory.aclose()\n    await s.relationship_store.close()\n    await s.pg_episodic.close()\n    s.event_log.emit(\"shutdown\", \"xnch\", \"SERVER_STOPPED\")\n\n\napp = FastAPI(title=\"xnch\", version=\"0.1.0\", lifespan=lifespan)\n\napp.include_router(session_router)\napp.include_router(memory_router)\napp.include_router(policy_router)\napp.include_router(verdict_router)\napp.include_router(execution_router)\napp.include_router(governance_router)\napp.include_router(auth_router)\napp.include_router(nexi_gateway_router)\n\n\n@app.get(\"/health\")\nasync def health(request: Request) -> dict:\n    redis_ok = await request.app.state.kv_cache.ping()\n    state_version = await request.app.state.get_state_version()\n    return {\n        \"status\": \"ok\" if redis_ok else \"degraded\",\n        \"redis\": \"ok\" if redis_ok else \"unavailable\",\n        \"state_version\": state_version,\n        \"version\": \"0.1.0\",\n    }\n\n\n@app.get(\"/system/state\")\nasync def system_state(request: Request) -> dict:\n    state_version = await request.app.state.get_state_version()\n    policy_version = await request.app.state.get_policy_version()\n    return {\"system_state_version\": state_version, \"policy_version\": policy_version}\n\n\ndef _sync_policies(s) -> None:\n    \"\"\"Copy bundled default policy to ~/.xnch/policies/ if not already present.\"\"\"\n    import pathlib, shutil\n    bundled = pathlib.Path(__file__).parent.parent.parent / \"policies\" / \"default.yaml\"\n    target = s.policies_dir / \"default.yaml\"\n    if bundled.exists() and not target.exists():\n        shutil.copy(bundled, target)\n","filePath":"/Users/xnch/xnchSystems/xnch/xnch/main.py","numLines":176,"startLine":1,"totalLines":176},"type":"text"}},"type":"raw"},"obs_mqv7gmta_0e4ae0e3be24":{"observation":{"hookType":"post_tool_use","id":"obs_mqv7gmta_0e4ae0e3be24","raw":{"tool_input":{"file_path":"/Users/xnch/xnchSystems/nexi/nexi/main.py"},"tool_name":"Read","tool_output":"{\"type\":\"text\",\"file\":{\"filePath\":\"/Users/xnch/xnchSystems/nexi/nexi/main.py\",\"content\":\"\\\"\\\"\\\"Nexi v0 — decision engine FastAPI application.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\nimport asyncio\\nimport logging\\nfrom contextlib import asynccontextmanager\\nfrom typing import Any\\nfrom uuid import UUID, uuid4\\n\\nfrom fastapi import FastAPI, HTTPException, BackgroundTasks\\nfrom fastapi.responses import JSONResponse as JSONResponse\\nfrom pydantic import BaseModel\\n\\nfrom .adapters import XnchClient, ModelAdapter\\nfrom .config import settings\\nfrom .models import SessionContext\\nfrom .pipeline import (\\n    IntentInterpreter, ClarificationRequired,\\n    load_context,\\n    generate_options,\\n    PolicyFilter, AllOptionsBlocked,\\n    Evaluator,\\n    select_decision,\\n    compile_action_spec, PlanCompilationError,\\n    dispatch_execution,\\n)\\nfrom .pipeline.dispatch import TokenExpired\\nfrom .utils.audit import emit_event\\n\\nlogger = logging.getLogger(__name__)\\n\\n\\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\\n# App lifecycle\\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\\n\\n_xnch: XnchClient | None = None\\n_model_adapter: ModelAdapter | None = None\\n_policy_filter: PolicyFilter | None = None\\n_intent_interpreter: IntentInterpreter | None = None\\n\\n\\n@asynccontextmanager\\nasync def lifespan(app: FastAPI):\\n    global _xnch, _model_adapter, _policy_filter, _intent_interpreter\\n    _xnch = XnchClient()\\n    _model_adapter = ModelAdapter()\\n    _policy_filter = PolicyFilter(_xnch)\\n    _intent_interpreter = IntentInterpreter()\\n    yield\\n    await _xnch.aclose()\\n\\n\\napp = FastAPI(title=\\\"Nexi\\\", version=\\\"0.1.0\\\", lifespan=lifespan)\\n\\n\\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\\n# Request / response schemas\\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\\n\\nclass SessionStartRequest(BaseModel):\\n    session_id: UUID\\n    trace_id: UUID\\n    actor: dict[str, Any]\\n    system_state_version: str\\n    policy_version: str\\n    raw_input: str\\n    priority: str = \\\"NORMAL\\\"\\n    idempotency_key: UUID\\n\\n\\nclass SessionStartResponse(BaseModel):\\n    status: str\\n    decision_id: UUID | None = None\\n    execution_ref: UUID | None = None\\n    estimated_completion_ms: int | None = None\\n    audit_ref: UUID | None = None\\n    clarification_required: bool = False\\n    hold_id: UUID | None = None\\n    error: str | None = None\\n\\n\\nclass ClarifyRequest(BaseModel):\\n    amended_input: str\\n\\n\\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\\n# Endpoints\\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\\n\\n@app.post(\\\"/session/start\\\", response_model=SessionStartResponse)\\nasync def session_start(\\n    body: SessionStartRequest,\\n    background_tasks: BackgroundTasks,\\n) -> SessionStartResponse:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Entry point called by xnch after actor resolution (Step 2 → Step 3).\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    session = SessionContext.model_validate(body.model_dump())\\n    emit_event(session.trace_id, \\\"nexi\\\", \\\"SESSION_START_RECEIVED\\\",\\n               {\\\"session_id\\\": str(session.session_id)})\\n\\n    if _intent_interpreter is None:\\n        return SessionStartResponse(status=\\\"ERROR\\\", error=\\\"intent interpreter not available\\\")\\n\\n    # Step 3 — Intent interpretation\\n    try:\\n        intent = await _intent_interpreter.interpret(\\n            body.raw_input, session.session_id, str(session.trace_id)\\n        )\\n    except ClarificationRequired as exc:\\n        return SessionStartResponse(\\n            status=\\\"CLARIFICATION_REQUIRED\\\",\\n            clarification_required=True,\\n        )\\n\\n    # Step 4 — Context manifest (hard stop on failure)\\n    try:\\n        manifest = await load_context(_xnch, session, intent)\\n    except Exception as exc:\\n        logger.error(\\\"Context manifest load failed: %s\\\", exc)\\n        raise HTTPException(status_code=503, detail=\\\"DEGRADED: context manifest unavailable\\\")\\n\\n    # Fetch weight config for this intent class (cached per session)\\n    try:\\n        weight_config = await _xnch.get_weight_config(intent.intent_class)\\n    except Exception:\\n        weight_config = None\\n\\n    evaluator = Evaluator(weight_config)\\n\\n    # Step 5 — Option generation\\n    n = settings.options_count\\n    raw_options, generation_path = await generate_options(\\n        _model_adapter, session, intent, manifest, n\\n    )\\n\\n    # Step 6 — Policy alignment filter\\n    try:\\n        surviving = await _policy_filter.filter(session, raw_options)\\n    except AllOptionsBlocked:\\n        hold_id = uuid4()\\n        emit_event(str(session.trace_id), \\\"nexi\\\", \\\"ESCALATED_ALL_BLOCKED\\\",\\n                   {\\\"hold_id\\\": str(hold_id)})\\n        return SessionStartResponse(status=\\\"ESCALATED\\\", hold_id=hold_id)\\n\\n    # Step 7 — Scoring\\n    evaluated = evaluator.score(surviving, intent, manifest, session)\\n\\n    # Step 8 — Outcome simulation (conditional)\\n    evaluated = evaluator.simulate_and_rescore(evaluated, surviving, manifest, intent, session)\\n\\n    # Step 9 — Selection\\n    n_blocked = len(raw_options) - len(surviving)\\n    decision = select_decision(\\n        session, intent, manifest,\\n        [opt for opt, _ in surviving], evaluated,\\n        n_generated=len(raw_options),\\n        n_blocked=n_blocked,\\n        generation_path=generation_path,\\n    )\\n\\n    if decision.escalation_triggered:\\n        hold_id = uuid4()\\n        return SessionStartResponse(status=\\\"ESCALATED\\\", hold_id=hold_id)\\n\\n    # Step 10a — Plan compilation\\n    selected_opt = next(\\n        (opt for opt, _ in surviving if opt.option_id == decision.selected_option_id),\\n        None,\\n    )\\n    if selected_opt is None:\\n        raise HTTPException(status_code=500, detail=\\\"Selected option not found\\\")\\n\\n    try:\\n        compiled = compile_action_spec(selected_opt)\\n    except PlanCompilationError as exc:\\n        raise HTTPException(status_code=422, detail=str(exc))\\n\\n    if not compiled.nodes:\\n        return JSONResponse({'error': 'compiled DAG has no nodes'}, status_code=422)\\n    node = compiled.nodes[0]\\n    validated_action_spec = {\\n        \\\"type\\\": node.action_type,\\n        \\\"target\\\": node.target,\\n        \\\"params\\\": node.params,\\n    }\\n\\n    # Step 10 — Final verdict\\n    try:\\n        verdict = await _xnch.submit_verdict(\\n            session, decision, validated_action_spec, selected_opt.payload_hash\\n        )\\n    except Exception as exc:\\n        error_body = str(exc)\\n        if \\\"STALE_SESSION\\\" in error_body:\\n            raise HTTPException(status_code=409, detail=\\\"STALE_SESSION: restart required\\\")\\n        raise HTTPException(status_code=502, detail=f\\\"Verdict submission failed: {error_body}\\\")\\n\\n    if verdict.verdict == \\\"BLOCK\\\":\\n        hold_id = uuid4()\\n        return SessionStartResponse(status=\\\"ESCALATED\\\", hold_id=hold_id)\\n\\n    # Step 11 — Execution dispatch (async handoff)\\n    execution_runner_url = settings.xnch_base_url.replace(\\\"8001\\\", \\\"8001\\\")\\n    try:\\n        dispatch_payload = await dispatch_execution(\\n            session, decision, verdict, validated_action_spec, execution_runner_url\\n        )\\n    except TokenExpired:\\n        # Resubmit to xnch for a new token, same decision_id\\n        verdict = await _xnch.submit_verdict(\\n            session, decision, validated_action_spec, selected_opt.payload_hash\\n        )\\n        dispatch_payload = await dispatch_execution(\\n            session, decision, verdict, validated_action_spec, execution_runner_url\\n        )\\n\\n    # Step 12 — Intermediate response to user\\n    emit_event(str(session.trace_id), \\\"nexi\\\", \\\"EXECUTING\\\",\\n               {\\\"execution_ref\\\": str(dispatch_payload.execution_ref)})\\n\\n    # Step 14 callback is handled async when execution-runner posts to xnch /execution/outcome\\n    # and xnch fires our callback at POST /callback/outcome\\n\\n    return SessionStartResponse(\\n        status=\\\"EXECUTING\\\",\\n        decision_i...[truncated]"},"sessionId":"283b9ba1-0eba-4a0c-ba9d-0cf00eb4bc4b","timestamp":"2026-06-26T17:28:55.633Z","toolInput":{"file_path":"/Users/xnch/xnchSystems/nexi/nexi/main.py"},"toolName":"Read","toolOutput":"{\"type\":\"text\",\"file\":{\"filePath\":\"/Users/xnch/xnchSystems/nexi/nexi/main.py\",\"content\":\"\\\"\\\"\\\"Nexi v0 — decision engine FastAPI application.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\nimport asyncio\\nimport logging\\nfrom contextlib import asynccontextmanager\\nfrom typing import Any\\nfrom uuid import UUID, uuid4\\n\\nfrom fastapi import FastAPI, HTTPException, BackgroundTasks\\nfrom fastapi.responses import JSONResponse as JSONResponse\\nfrom pydantic import BaseModel\\n\\nfrom .adapters import XnchClient, ModelAdapter\\nfrom .config import settings\\nfrom .models import SessionContext\\nfrom .pipeline import (\\n    IntentInterpreter, ClarificationRequired,\\n    load_context,\\n    generate_options,\\n    PolicyFilter, AllOptionsBlocked,\\n    Evaluator,\\n    select_decision,\\n    compile_action_spec, PlanCompilationError,\\n    dispatch_execution,\\n)\\nfrom .pipeline.dispatch import TokenExpired\\nfrom .utils.audit import emit_event\\n\\nlogger = logging.getLogger(__name__)\\n\\n\\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\\n# App lifecycle\\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\\n\\n_xnch: XnchClient | None = None\\n_model_adapter: ModelAdapter | None = None\\n_policy_filter: PolicyFilter | None = None\\n_intent_interpreter: IntentInterpreter | None = None\\n\\n\\n@asynccontextmanager\\nasync def lifespan(app: FastAPI):\\n    global _xnch, _model_adapter, _policy_filter, _intent_interpreter\\n    _xnch = XnchClient()\\n    _model_adapter = ModelAdapter()\\n    _policy_filter = PolicyFilter(_xnch)\\n    _intent_interpreter = IntentInterpreter()\\n    yield\\n    await _xnch.aclose()\\n\\n\\napp = FastAPI(title=\\\"Nexi\\\", version=\\\"0.1.0\\\", lifespan=lifespan)\\n\\n\\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\\n# Request / response schemas\\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\\n\\nclass SessionStartRequest(BaseModel):\\n    session_id: UUID\\n    trace_id: UUID\\n    actor: dict[str, Any]\\n    system_state_version: str\\n    policy_version: str\\n    raw_input: str\\n    priority: str = \\\"NORMAL\\\"\\n    idempotency_key: UUID\\n\\n\\nclass SessionStartResponse(BaseModel):\\n    status: str\\n    decision_id: UUID | None = None\\n    execution_ref: UUID | None = None\\n    estimated_completion_ms: int | None = None\\n    audit_ref: UUID | None = None\\n    clarification_required: bool = False\\n    hold_id: UUID | None = None\\n    error: str | None = None\\n\\n\\nclass ClarifyRequest(BaseModel):\\n    amended_input: str\\n\\n\\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\\n# Endpoints\\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\\n\\n@app.post(\\\"/session/start\\\", response_model=SessionStartResponse)\\nasync def session_start(\\n    body: SessionStartRequest,\\n    background_tasks: BackgroundTasks,\\n) -> SessionStartResponse:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Entry point called by xnch after actor resolution (Step 2 → Step 3).\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    session = SessionContext.model_validate(body.model_dump())\\n    emit_event(session.trace_id, \\\"nexi\\\", \\\"SESSION_START_RECEIVED\\\",\\n               {\\\"session_id\\\": str(session.session_id)})\\n\\n    if _intent_interpreter is None:\\n        return SessionStartResponse(status=\\\"ERROR\\\", error=\\\"intent interpreter not available\\\")\\n\\n    # Step 3 — Intent interpretation\\n    try:\\n        intent = await _intent_interpreter.interpret(\\n            body.raw_input, session.session_id, str(session.trace_id)\\n        )\\n    except ClarificationRequired as exc:\\n        return SessionStartResponse(\\n            status=\\\"CLARIFICATION_REQUIRED\\\",\\n            clarification_required=True,\\n        )\\n\\n    # Step 4 — Context manifest (hard stop on failure)\\n    try:\\n        manifest = await load_context(_xnch, session, intent)\\n    except Exception as exc:\\n        logger.error(\\\"Context manifest load failed: %s\\\", exc)\\n        raise HTTPException(status_code=503, detail=\\\"DEGRADED: context manifest unavailable\\\")\\n\\n    # Fetch weight config for this intent class (cached per session)\\n    try:\\n        weight_config = await _xnch.get_weight_config(intent.intent_class)\\n    except Exception:\\n        weight_config = None\\n\\n    evaluator = Evaluator(weight_config)\\n\\n    # Step 5 — Option generation\\n    n = settings.options_count\\n    raw_options, generation_path = await generate_options(\\n        _model_adapter, session, intent, manifest, n\\n    )\\n\\n    # Step 6 — Policy alignment filter\\n    try:\\n        surviving = await _policy_filter.filter(session, raw_options)\\n    except AllOptionsBlocked:\\n        hold_id = uuid4()\\n        emit_event(str(session.trace_id), \\\"nexi\\\", \\\"ESCALATED_ALL_BLOCKED\\\",\\n                   {\\\"hold_id\\\": str(hold_id)})\\n        return SessionStartResponse(status=\\\"ESCALATED\\\", hold_id=hold_id)\\n\\n    # Step 7 — Scoring\\n    evaluated = evaluator.score(surviving, intent, manifest, session)\\n\\n    # Step 8 — Outcome simulation (conditional)\\n    evaluated = evaluator.simulate_and_rescore(evaluated, surviving, manifest, intent, session)\\n\\n    # Step 9 — Selection\\n    n_blocked = len(raw_options) - len(surviving)\\n    decision = select_decision(\\n        session, intent, manifest,\\n        [opt for opt, _ in surviving], evaluated,\\n        n_generated=len(raw_options),\\n        n_blocked=n_blocked,\\n        generation_path=generation_path,\\n    )\\n\\n    if decision.escalation_triggered:\\n        hold_id = uuid4()\\n        return SessionStartResponse(status=\\\"ESCALATED\\\", hold_id=hold_id)\\n\\n    # Step 10a — Plan compilation\\n    selected_opt = next(\\n        (opt for opt, _ in surviving if opt.option_id == decision.selected_option_id),\\n        None,\\n    )\\n    if selected_opt is None:\\n        raise HTTPException(status_code=500, detail=\\\"Selected option not found\\\")\\n\\n    try:\\n        compiled = compile_action_spec(selected_opt)\\n    except PlanCompilationError as exc:\\n        raise HTTPException(status_code=422, detail=str(exc))\\n\\n    if not compiled.nodes:\\n        return JSONResponse({'error': 'compiled DAG has no nodes'}, status_code=422)\\n    node = compiled.nodes[0]\\n    validated_action_spec = {\\n        \\\"type\\\": node.action_type,\\n        \\\"target\\\": node.target,\\n        \\\"params\\\": node.params,\\n    }\\n\\n    # Step 10 — Final verdict\\n    try:\\n        verdict = await _xnch.submit_verdict(\\n            session, decision, validated_action_spec, selected_opt.payload_hash\\n        )\\n    except Exception as exc:\\n        error_body = str(exc)\\n        if \\\"STALE_SESSION\\\" in error_body:\\n            raise HTTPException(status_code=409, detail=\\\"STALE_SESSION: restart required\\\")\\n        raise HTTPException(status_code=502, detail=f\\\"Verdict submission failed: {error_body}\\\")\\n\\n    if verdict.verdict == \\\"BLOCK\\\":\\n        hold_id = uuid4()\\n        return SessionStartResponse(status=\\\"ESCALATED\\\", hold_id=hold_id)\\n\\n    # Step 11 — Execution dispatch (async handoff)\\n    execution_runner_url = settings.xnch_base_url.replace(\\\"8001\\\", \\\"8001\\\")\\n    try:\\n        dispatch_payload = await dispatch_execution(\\n            session, decision, verdict, validated_action_spec, execution_runner_url\\n        )\\n    except TokenExpired:\\n        # Resubmit to xnch for a new token, same decision_id\\n        verdict = await _xnch.submit_verdict(\\n        