_bab8cd1f6935","raw":{"tool_input":{"command":".venv/bin/pytest --tb=short -q 2>&1 | tail -8","description":"Full suite run after all fixes","timeout":120000},"tool_name":"Bash","tool_output":{"interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"stderr":"","stdout":"    decoded = self.decode_complete(\n\nxnch/tests/test_auth.py::TestTokenVerifier::test_wrong_signature_returns_none\n  /Users/xnch/xnchSystems/.venv/lib/python3.13/site-packages/jwt/api_jwt.py:147: InsecureKeyLengthWarning: The HMAC key is 29 bytes long, which is below the minimum recommended length of 32 bytes for SHA256. See RFC 7518 Section 3.2.\n    return self._jws.encode(\n\n-- Docs: https://docs.pytest.org/en/stable/how-to/capture-warnings.html\n244 passed, 12 warnings in 9.72s"}},"sessionId":"283b9ba1-0eba-4a0c-ba9d-0cf00eb4bc4b","timestamp":"2026-06-26T18:33:47.366Z","toolInput":{"command":".venv/bin/pytest --tb=short -q 2>&1 | tail -8","description":"Full suite run after all fixes","timeout":120000},"toolName":"Bash","toolOutput":{"interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"stderr":"","stdout":"    decoded = self.decode_complete(\n\nxnch/tests/test_auth.py::TestTokenVerifier::test_wrong_signature_returns_none\n  /Users/xnch/xnchSystems/.venv/lib/python3.13/site-packages/jwt/api_jwt.py:147: InsecureKeyLengthWarning: The HMAC key is 29 bytes long, which is below the minimum recommended length of 32 bytes for SHA256. See RFC 7518 Section 3.2.\n    return self._jws.encode(\n\n-- Docs: https://docs.pytest.org/en/stable/how-to/capture-warnings.html\n244 passed, 12 warnings in 9.72s"}},"type":"raw"},"obs_mqv9t40s_b1f517ef4424":{"observation":{"hookType":"prompt_submit","id":"obs_mqv9t40s_b1f517ef4424","raw":{"prompt":"/agentmemory:remember update to agentmemory"},"sessionId":"283b9ba1-0eba-4a0c-ba9d-0cf00eb4bc4b","timestamp":"2026-06-26T18:34:37.016Z","userPrompt":"/agentmemory:remember update to agentmemory"},"type":"raw"},"obs_mqv9tg7r_a4a3fe27b0ef":{"observation":{"hookType":"post_tool_use","id":"obs_mqv9tg7r_a4a3fe27b0ef","raw":{"tool_input":{"concepts":"agentmemory-singleton-reset, chromadb-test-isolation, conftest-storage-path, mock-spec-isinstance, kv-cache-redis-client-mock","content":"agentmemory uses a module-level client singleton (`agentmemory.client.client`). When tests set STORAGE_PATH per-test and delete the temp dir at teardown, the singleton keeps pointing to the deleted path — causing `SQLITE_READONLY_CANTINIT` errors in subsequent tests. Fix: reset `import agentmemory.client as _am_client; _am_client.client = None` before AND after each test in conftest.py fixtures. The nexi/tests/conftest.py `_isolate_chromadb` fixture was missing this reset; tests/conftest.py needed the same pattern added. Also: `requires_trust` decorator uses `isinstance(arg, Request)` (not `hasattr`) — test mocks must use `MagicMock(spec=Request)` to pass the isinstance check. And `kv_cache.redis_client` (property) must be mocked directly on the MagicMock, not via `kv_cache._redis`.","files":"nexi/tests/conftest.py, tests/conftest.py, tests/security/test_trust_model.py, tests/test_nexi_gateway.py","project":"xnchSystems","type":"pattern"},"tool_name":"mcp__plugin_agentmemory_agentmemory__memory_save","tool_output":[{"text":"{\"memory\":{\"concepts\":[\"agentmemory-singleton-reset\",\"chromadb-test-isolation\",\"conftest-storage-path\",\"mock-spec-isinstance\",\"kv-cache-redis-client-mock\"],\"content\":\"agentmemory uses a module-level client singleton (`agentmemory.client.client`). When tests set STORAGE_PATH per-test and delete the temp dir at teardown, the singleton keeps pointing to the deleted path — causing `SQLITE_READONLY_CANTINIT` errors in subsequent tests. Fix: reset `import agentmemory.client as _am_client; _am_client.client = None` before AND after each test in conftest.py fixtures. The nexi/tests/conftest.py `_isolate_chromadb` fixture was missing this reset; tests/conftest.py needed the same pattern added. Also: `requires_trust` decorator uses `isinstance(arg, Request)` (not `hasattr`) — test mocks must use `MagicMock(spec=Request)` to pass the isinstance check. And `kv_cache.redis_client` (property) must be mocked directly on the MagicMock, not via `kv_cache._redis`.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-06-26T18:34:52.669Z\",\"files\":[\"nexi/tests/conftest.py\",\"tests/conftest.py\",\"tests/security/test_trust_model.py\",\"tests/test_nexi_gateway.py\"],\"id\":\"mem_mqv9tg1t_f5a100ba328f\",\"isLatest\":true,\"sessionIds\":[],\"sourceObservationIds\":[],\"strength\":7,\"supersedes\":[],\"title\":\"agentmemory uses a module-level client singleton (`agentmemory.client.client`). \",\"type\":\"pattern\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-06-26T18:34:52.669Z\",\"version\":1},\"success\":true}","type":"text"}]},"sessionId":"283b9ba1-0eba-4a0c-ba9d-0cf00eb4bc4b","timestamp":"2026-06-26T18:34:52.843Z","toolInput":{"concepts":"agentmemory-singleton-reset, chromadb-test-isolation, conftest-storage-path, mock-spec-isinstance, kv-cache-redis-client-mock","content":"agentmemory uses a module-level client singleton (`agentmemory.client.client`). When tests set STORAGE_PATH per-test and delete the temp dir at teardown, the singleton keeps pointing to the deleted path — causing `SQLITE_READONLY_CANTINIT` errors in subsequent tests. Fix: reset `import agentmemory.client as _am_client; _am_client.client = None` before AND after each test in conftest.py fixtures. The nexi/tests/conftest.py `_isolate_chromadb` fixture was missing this reset; tests/conftest.py needed the same pattern added. Also: `requires_trust` decorator uses `isinstance(arg, Request)` (not `hasattr`) — test mocks must use `MagicMock(spec=Request)` to pass the isinstance check. And `kv_cache.redis_client` (property) must be mocked directly on the MagicMock, not via `kv_cache._redis`.","files":"nexi/tests/conftest.py, tests/conftest.py, tests/security/test_trust_model.py, tests/test_nexi_gateway.py","project":"xnchSystems","type":"pattern"},"toolName":"mcp__plugin_agentmemory_agentmemory__memory_save","toolOutput":[{"text":"{\"memory\":{\"concepts\":[\"agentmemory-singleton-reset\",\"chromadb-test-isolation\",\"conftest-storage-path\",\"mock-spec-isinstance\",\"kv-cache-redis-client-mock\"],\"content\":\"agentmemory uses a module-level client singleton (`agentmemory.client.client`). When tests set STORAGE_PATH per-test and delete the temp dir at teardown, the singleton keeps pointing to the deleted path — causing `SQLITE_READONLY_CANTINIT` errors in subsequent tests. Fix: reset `import agentmemory.client as _am_client; _am_client.client = None` before AND after each test in conftest.py fixtures. The nexi/tests/conftest.py `_isolate_chromadb` fixture was missing this reset; tests/conftest.py needed the same pattern added. Also: `requires_trust` decorator uses `isinstance(arg, Request)` (not `hasattr`) — test mocks must use `MagicMock(spec=Request)` to pass the isinstance check. And `kv_cache.redis_client` (property) must be mocked directly on the MagicMock, not via `kv_cache._redis`.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-06-26T18:34:52.669Z\",\"files\":[\"nexi/tests/conftest.py\",\"tests/conftest.py\",\"tests/security/test_trust_model.py\",\"tests/test_nexi_gateway.py\"],\"id\":\"mem_mqv9tg1t_f5a100ba328f\",\"isLatest\":true,\"sessionIds\":[],\"sourceObservationIds\":[],\"strength\":7,\"supersedes\":[],\"title\":\"agentmemory uses a module-level client singleton (`agentmemory.client.client`). \",\"type\":\"pattern\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-06-26T18:34:52.669Z\",\"version\":1},\"success\":true}","type":"text"}]},"type":"raw"},"obs_mqv9tkup_ab55dcb9242c":{"observation":{"hookType":"subagent_stop","id":"obs_mqv9tkup_ab55dcb9242c","raw":{"agent_id":"a6ef8e68190a3ac09","last_message":"commit this"},"sessionId":"283b9ba1-0eba-4a0c-ba9d-0cf00eb4bc4b","timestamp":"2026-06-26T18:34:58.856Z"},"type":"raw"}}␀�␀x���